WEBVTT

02:01.000 --> 02:02.059
- Captain.
- Yes, sir?

02:03.136 --> 02:05.263
Tell them we wish
to board at once.

02:05.372 --> 02:08.000
- [Machinery Beeping]
- With all due respect,

02:08.108 --> 02:11.545
the ambassadors for the supreme
chancellor wish to board immediately.

02:11.646 --> 02:13.546
Yes, of course.

02:13.681 --> 02:16.741
As you know, our blockade
is perfectly legal,

02:16.884 --> 02:20.912
and we'd be happy
to receive the ambassadors.

02:43.415 --> 02:46.043
I'm TC-14
at your service.

02:46.184 --> 02:48.084
This way, please.

02:54.193 --> 02:57.288
We are greatly honored
by your visit, Ambassadors.

02:57.397 --> 02:59.297
Make yourselves
comfortable.

02:59.399 --> 03:02.562
My master will be
with you shortly.

03:05.573 --> 03:07.871
I have a bad feeling
about this.

03:07.975 --> 03:11.001
- I don't sense anything.
- It's not about the mission, Master.

03:11.112 --> 03:15.049
It's something...
elsewhere, elusive.

03:15.150 --> 03:17.550
Don't center on
your anxieties, Obi-Wan.

03:17.653 --> 03:20.817
Keep your concentration
here and now, where it belongs.

03:20.957 --> 03:23.790
But Master Yoda said
I should be mindful of the future.

03:23.893 --> 03:25.884
But not at the expense
of the moment.

03:26.029 --> 03:28.999
Be mindful of the living Force,
young Padawan.

03:29.100 --> 03:31.000
Yes, Master.

03:33.204 --> 03:36.868
How do you think this trade viceroy
will deal with the chancellor's demands?

03:36.975 --> 03:39.068
These Federation types
are cowards.

03:39.177 --> 03:42.044
The negotiations
will be short.

03:42.147 --> 03:45.447
What?
What did you say?

03:45.551 --> 03:48.520
The ambassadors are Jedi knights,
I believe.

03:48.621 --> 03:50.521
I knew it.

03:50.623 --> 03:52.854
They're here
to force a settlement.

03:52.993 --> 03:57.020
Distract them.
I will contact Lord Sidious.

03:57.164 --> 03:59.065
Are you brain-dead?

03:59.167 --> 04:03.069
I'm not going in there
with two Jedi.

04:03.171 --> 04:05.071
Send a droid.

04:09.545 --> 04:12.378
Is it in their nature
to make us wait this long?

04:12.481 --> 04:17.044
No. I sense an unusual amount of fear
for something as trivial
as this trade dispute.

04:28.032 --> 04:29.933
What is it?

04:30.035 --> 04:32.663
This scheme of yours
has failed, Lord Sidious.

04:32.805 --> 04:36.366
The blockade is finished.
We dare not go against these Jedi.

04:36.475 --> 04:41.311
Viceroy, I don't want
this stunted slime in my sight again.

04:42.649 --> 04:45.174
This turn of events
is unfortunate.

04:45.285 --> 04:49.382
We must accelerate our plans.
Begin landing your troops.

04:49.490 --> 04:53.222
My lord,
is that legal?

04:53.328 --> 04:55.626
I will make it legal.

04:55.730 --> 04:58.062
And the Jedi?

04:58.166 --> 05:02.604
The chancellor should never have brought
them into this. Kill them immediately.

05:02.705 --> 05:07.005
Yes. Yes, my lord.
Uh, as you wish.

05:08.846 --> 05:10.677
Captain, look!

05:10.781 --> 05:13.147
Shields up!

05:16.654 --> 05:18.519
Sorry.

05:20.258 --> 05:22.158
Dioxis.

05:26.999 --> 05:29.627
They must be dead by now.

05:29.735 --> 05:33.672
Destroy what's left of them.

05:40.548 --> 05:42.982
Oh! Excuse me.

05:43.084 --> 05:46.053
- Check it out, Corporal.
We'll cover you.
- Roger, roger.

05:46.153 --> 05:48.645
Uh-oh. Blast them.

05:53.629 --> 05:55.962
What is going on
down there?

05:56.065 --> 05:58.033
We lost the transmission,
sir.

06:02.505 --> 06:05.532
Have you ever encountered
a Jedi knight before, sir?

06:05.643 --> 06:08.635
Well, no, but I don't...
Seal off the bridge.

06:08.746 --> 06:11.443
- Yes, sir.
- That won't be enough, sir.

06:11.583 --> 06:13.551
I want droidekas
up here at once!

06:13.685 --> 06:16.176
We will not
survive this.

06:24.797 --> 06:26.629
[Whining]

06:27.768 --> 06:30.168
Close the blast doors!

06:35.143 --> 06:37.976
That will hold them.

06:46.488 --> 06:49.218
They are still
coming through.

06:49.325 --> 06:51.226
This is impossible!

06:55.732 --> 06:58.531
Where are
those droidekas?

07:00.137 --> 07:01.866
Master! Destroyers!

07:08.313 --> 07:11.043
They have shield
generators!

07:11.149 --> 07:13.846
It's a standoff.
Let's go.

07:18.057 --> 07:20.548
They're no match
for droidekas.

07:20.693 --> 07:25.131
Sir! They've gone up
the ventilation shaft.

07:33.875 --> 07:36.537
- Battle droids.
- It's an invasion army.

07:38.314 --> 07:40.976
This is an odd play
for the Trade Federation.

07:41.083 --> 07:44.211
We've got to warn the Naboo
and contact Chancellor Valorum.

07:44.320 --> 07:49.258
Let's split up. Stow aboard separate
ships and meet down on the planet.

07:49.359 --> 07:52.261
You were right
about one thing, Master.

07:52.363 --> 07:55.855
The negotiations
were short.

07:56.067 --> 07:59.434
Sir, a transmission
from the planet.

07:59.537 --> 08:01.631
It's Queen Amidala herself.

08:01.740 --> 08:05.437
At last we are
getting results.

08:05.511 --> 08:08.504
Again you come before us,
Your Highness.

08:08.615 --> 08:11.743
You will not be so pleased when you hear
what I have to say, Viceroy.

08:11.851 --> 08:15.582
Your trade boycott
of our planet has ended.

08:15.689 --> 08:18.249
I was not aware
of such failure.

08:18.359 --> 08:21.089
I have word that the chancellor's
ambassadors are with you now...

08:21.228 --> 08:23.891
and that you have been commanded
to reach settlement.

08:24.032 --> 08:26.330
I know nothing
of any ambassadors.

08:26.435 --> 08:28.835
You must be mistaken.

08:28.937 --> 08:30.962
Beware, Viceroy.

08:31.073 --> 08:33.770
The Federation
has gone too far this time.

08:33.876 --> 08:37.937
We would never do anything
without the approval of the senate.

08:38.047 --> 08:40.539
You assume too much.

08:40.651 --> 08:43.552
We will see.

08:43.654 --> 08:47.682
- She's right. The senate will never...
- It's too late now.

08:47.792 --> 08:50.761
- Do you think she suspects an attack?
- I don't know.

08:50.862 --> 08:55.266
But we must move quickly to disrupt
all communications down there.

09:00.139 --> 09:04.543
Negotiations haven't started
because the ambassadors aren't there?

09:04.644 --> 09:06.805
How could that be true?

09:06.913 --> 09:11.283
I have assurances from the chancellor
his ambassadors did arrive.

09:11.385 --> 09:15.116
[Distorted Voice] It must...
handiwork... negotiate... ambassadors...

09:15.223 --> 09:17.885
- Nobody would...
- Senator Palpatine.

09:17.993 --> 09:19.893
What's happening?

09:19.995 --> 09:21.895
Check the transmission
generator.

09:21.997 --> 09:26.901
A communications disruption
can mean only one thing: invasion.

09:27.036 --> 09:29.300
The Federation would not
dare go that far.

09:29.439 --> 09:33.273
The senate would revoke their
trade franchise, and they'd be finished.

09:33.376 --> 09:36.244
We must continue to rely
on negotiation.

09:36.347 --> 09:39.578
Negotiation?
We've lost all communications.

09:39.683 --> 09:42.016
And where are
the chancellor's ambassadors?

09:43.355 --> 09:45.789
This is a dangerous situation,
Your Highness.

09:45.891 --> 09:50.261
Our security volunteers
will be no match against
a battle-hardened Federation army.

09:51.831 --> 09:56.495
I will not condone a course of action
that will lead us to war.

10:31.976 --> 10:35.104
- Yes, Viceroy?
- Captain, we've searched the ship,

10:35.246 --> 10:37.340
and there is no trace
of the Jedi.

10:37.482 --> 10:40.246
They may have gotten on
one of your landing craft.

10:40.352 --> 10:42.820
If they're down here, sir,
we'll find them.

10:42.955 --> 10:47.791
Use caution.
These Jedi are not to be underestimated.

10:47.894 --> 10:50.829
[Howling]

10:53.634 --> 10:56.501
[Creatures Snorting, Squawking]

11:01.076 --> 11:03.670
- Oh, no!
- Get away! Get out of here!

11:03.778 --> 11:06.770
- Get down!
- [Whimpering]

11:06.916 --> 11:09.111
Ay-yee-yee! Wha!

11:15.726 --> 11:19.321
Was'n dat?
Hey, wait!

11:19.496 --> 11:21.327
Oh, mooie-mooie!
I love you!

11:21.431 --> 11:23.627
You almost got us killed.
Are you brainless?

11:23.735 --> 11:27.432
- I spake.
- The ability to speak does
not make you intelligent.

11:27.538 --> 11:30.440
- Now, get out of here.
- No, no, mesa stay.

11:30.542 --> 11:33.602
Mesa culled JarJar Binks.
Mesa your humble servant.

11:33.712 --> 11:35.839
- That won't be necessary.
- Oh, but it 'tis.

11:35.948 --> 11:38.850
'Tis demanded
by the gods, it 'tis.

11:38.952 --> 11:42.410
- Oh, no! Whoo!
- Stay down!

11:48.396 --> 11:50.990
You saved my again.

11:51.098 --> 11:52.998
- What's this?
- A local.

11:53.100 --> 11:56.832
- Let's get out of here
before more droids show up.
- More?

11:56.938 --> 11:59.168
" More" did you spake?

11:59.274 --> 12:04.144
Ex-squeeze-me, but de mostest
safest place would be Gunga City.

12:04.247 --> 12:07.478
Is where I grew up.
'Tis a hidden city.

12:09.085 --> 12:10.986
- A city?
- Uh-huh.

12:11.088 --> 12:15.252
- Can you take us there?
- Uh, on second thought, no.

12:15.392 --> 12:17.861
- Not really, no.
- No?

12:17.996 --> 12:20.089
'Tis embarrassing,

12:20.231 --> 12:24.167
but, uh, my afraid
my've been banished.

12:24.302 --> 12:27.431
My forgotten.
Da bosses would do terrible tings to me.

12:27.540 --> 12:30.634
- Terrible tings to me
if me goen back dare.
-[Rumbling Sound]

12:30.743 --> 12:33.736
- You hear that?
- Yah.

12:33.847 --> 12:37.613
That is the sound of a thousand
terrible things heading this way.

12:37.718 --> 12:40.278
If they find us,
they will crush us,

12:40.388 --> 12:44.950
grind us into tiny pieces
and blast us into oblivion.

12:45.059 --> 12:49.019
Oh. Yousa point
is well seen.

12:49.131 --> 12:51.497
This way. Hurry!

12:51.600 --> 12:56.664
[Creatures Chittering, Hooting]

12:56.773 --> 13:00.072
- How much further?
- Wesa goen underwater, okeyday?

13:00.176 --> 13:02.076
Ah, my warning you.

13:02.178 --> 13:06.309
Gungans no liken outsiders,
so don't spect a warm welcome.

13:06.417 --> 13:09.750
Oh, don't worry. This hasn't
been our day for warm welcomes.

13:09.854 --> 13:13.757
Ar, ar, ar!
Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh!

13:20.199 --> 13:22.633
Yousa follow me now,
okeyday?

14:07.953 --> 14:10.854
[JarJar]
So good bein home!

14:10.956 --> 14:14.415
[Gasping, Chattering]

14:17.030 --> 14:18.998
- Oh, me gusa.
- Hata-hata.

14:21.936 --> 14:25.667
[Chattering Continues]

14:25.773 --> 14:28.105
- [Creature Growling]
- Hey, yousa.

14:28.242 --> 14:32.270
- Stopa dare!
- Heyo-dales, Cap'n Tarpals.

14:32.414 --> 14:34.314
Mesa back!

14:34.416 --> 14:37.352
Noah gain, JarJar.
Yousa goen tada bosses.

14:37.453 --> 14:40.115
Yousa in big dudu
dis time.

14:40.223 --> 14:41.747
Ohh.

14:41.858 --> 14:44.224
Ay, ay.

14:44.327 --> 14:47.456
[Gasps]
How wude.

14:47.564 --> 14:49.464
[Grunts]

14:54.105 --> 14:58.542
Tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk!
Yousa cannot bees hair.

14:58.643 --> 15:03.172
Dis army of Mackineeks
up dare is new weesong.

15:03.315 --> 15:08.218
A droid army is about to attack
the Naboo. We must warn them.

15:08.321 --> 15:11.950
Wesa no like da Naboo.
Tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk-tkk.

15:12.058 --> 15:14.856
Da Naboo tink
day so smarty.

15:14.961 --> 15:17.897
Day tink
day brains so big.

15:17.999 --> 15:22.129
Once those droids take control of the
surface, they will take control of you.

15:22.236 --> 15:24.535
Mesa no tink so.

15:24.640 --> 15:27.541
Day not know of uss-en.

15:27.643 --> 15:30.612
You and the Naboo form
a symbiont circle.

15:30.712 --> 15:34.114
What happens to one of you will affect
the other. You must understand this.

15:34.250 --> 15:39.051
Wesa no carrrre-nn
about da Naboo.

15:39.155 --> 15:41.681
Then speed us on our way.

15:41.825 --> 15:44.316
Wesa ganna
speed yous away.

15:44.461 --> 15:47.260
We could use a transport.

15:47.365 --> 15:50.232
Wesa give yousa
una bongo.

15:50.335 --> 15:53.395
- Hmm?
- Da speediest way tooda Naboo...

15:53.505 --> 15:58.239
'tis goen through
the planet core.

15:58.344 --> 16:00.244
Now...

16:00.346 --> 16:02.177
go.

16:02.281 --> 16:04.546
Thank you for your help.
We leave in peace.

16:04.651 --> 16:06.710
Master, what's a bongo?

16:06.853 --> 16:08.821
A transport, I hope.

16:08.956 --> 16:11.016
Deysa setten
yousa up.

16:11.159 --> 16:14.788
Goen through da planet core?
Bad bombin'.

16:14.896 --> 16:19.095
Mmm... any help here
would be hot.

16:20.402 --> 16:22.302
Master,
we're short on time.

16:22.404 --> 16:26.033
We'll need a navigator
to get us through the planet's core.

16:26.141 --> 16:28.110
This Gungan
may be of help.

16:30.213 --> 16:33.273
What is to become
ofJarJar Binks here?

16:33.383 --> 16:38.321
Hisen soon to be
pune-ished.

16:38.422 --> 16:40.652
- Ohh.
- I saved his life.

16:40.791 --> 16:43.260
He owes me what you call
a " life-debt."

16:43.395 --> 16:47.263
Your gods demand that his life
belongs to me now.

16:47.366 --> 16:49.733
Binkssssss,

16:49.836 --> 16:53.431
yousa havena liveplay
with thisen hisen?

16:53.539 --> 16:56.940
Mm, uh-huh.

16:57.043 --> 17:00.411
[Loud Blubbering]

17:00.514 --> 17:02.345
Begone wit him!

17:05.019 --> 17:07.420
Count me outta
dis one.

17:07.522 --> 17:10.650
Better dead here
than dead in da core.

17:10.759 --> 17:13.923
Yee gods!
What mesa sayin?

17:20.036 --> 17:22.471
[Engine Humming]

17:32.150 --> 17:34.948
Dis is nutsen.
Oh, gooberfish!

17:35.053 --> 17:38.319
- Why were you banished, JarJar?
- It's a longo tale-o,

17:38.424 --> 17:43.487
buta small part of it
would be mesa... clumsy.

17:43.595 --> 17:48.397
- You were banished
because you were clumsy?
- Yousa might'n be sayin dat.

18:01.349 --> 18:05.581
Mesa caused mabbe one,
two-y lettle bitty axadentes, huh?

18:05.654 --> 18:07.748
Yud-say
boom da gassar,

18:07.857 --> 18:10.655
den crashin der boss's heyblibber,
den banished.

18:14.864 --> 18:17.800
- Wuh-oh!
- [Growling]

18:17.901 --> 18:19.960
Big gooberfish!
Huge-o teeth!

18:25.110 --> 18:27.010
[Roaring]

18:30.816 --> 18:34.912
- There's always a bigger fish.
- Mesa tink we goen back now.

18:35.020 --> 18:38.148
[Roaring]

18:42.662 --> 18:46.154
[Engines Howling]

18:46.266 --> 18:49.498
The invasion is on schedule,
my lord.

18:49.604 --> 18:52.596
I have the senate bogged down
in procedures.

18:52.707 --> 18:57.168
They will have no choice but to accept
your control of the system.

18:57.279 --> 19:02.013
The queen has great faith
that the senate will side with her.

19:02.118 --> 19:05.110
Queen Amidala
is young and naive.

19:05.221 --> 19:08.679
You will find controlling her
will not be difficult.

19:08.792 --> 19:10.693
Yes, my lord.

19:12.129 --> 19:14.996
You didn't tell him
about the missing Jedi.

19:15.099 --> 19:19.628
No need to report that to him
until we have something to report.

19:24.109 --> 19:27.876
- Where wesa goin?
- Don't worry. The Force will guide us.

19:28.014 --> 19:30.778
Ohh, maxi big, da Force.

19:30.917 --> 19:33.716
Well, dat smells
stinkowiff.

19:33.821 --> 19:35.721
-[Alarm Blaring]
- We're losing power.

19:35.823 --> 19:37.484
[Whimpers]
Ohhh, no!

19:43.431 --> 19:45.661
Wesa dyin' here.
[Sobbing]

19:45.767 --> 19:48.463
- Just relax. We're not in trouble yet.
- What "yet"?

19:48.570 --> 19:51.563
Monsters out dare.
Leak'n in here.

19:51.674 --> 19:56.612
All sink'n and no power?
Whena yousa tinkin wesa in trouble?

19:57.914 --> 20:00.246
- Power's back.
- Huh?

20:00.350 --> 20:02.409
Aah, monster's back!
[Blubbering]

20:02.552 --> 20:04.578
[Roars]

20:09.360 --> 20:11.624
- [Whimpering]
- Relax.

20:11.729 --> 20:13.630
- Ohh.
- You overdid it.

20:15.000 --> 20:17.298
[Growling]

20:20.506 --> 20:22.497
[Roaring]

20:28.582 --> 20:31.380
- Horrible.
- Head for that outcropping.

20:31.485 --> 20:34.477
[Blubbers]
Oh, boy.

21:09.828 --> 21:11.887
Viceroy, we have
captured the queen.

21:12.031 --> 21:14.694
Ah, victory.

21:24.745 --> 21:27.236
[Birds Squawking]

21:27.348 --> 21:30.341
Mmm, dis'n loverly.

21:30.452 --> 21:32.852
[Engine Powering Down]

21:35.524 --> 21:38.892
How will you explain
this invasion to the senate?

21:38.995 --> 21:43.193
The queen and I will sign a treaty that
will legitimize our occupation here.

21:43.333 --> 21:46.462
I have assurances
it will be ratified by the senate.

21:46.603 --> 21:50.061
- I will not cooperate.
- Now, now, Your Highness.

21:50.207 --> 21:54.338
I n time, the suffering of your people
will persuade you to see
our point of view.

21:55.680 --> 21:57.614
- Commander.
- Yes, sir.

21:57.716 --> 22:01.244
- Process them.
- Captain, take them to Camp 4.

22:01.354 --> 22:03.254
Roger, roger.

22:43.601 --> 22:46.195
Whoops!

22:46.303 --> 22:48.772
[JarJar]
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

22:57.850 --> 23:01.843
- We should leave the street,
Your Highness.
- Get their weapons.

23:01.954 --> 23:05.413
Whoa!
Yousa guys bombad!

23:07.494 --> 23:09.894
We're ambassadors
for the supreme chancellor.

23:09.997 --> 23:11.932
Your negotiations seemed
to have failed, Ambassador.

23:12.033 --> 23:13.864
The negotiations
never took place.

23:13.968 --> 23:16.368
It's urgent that we make contact
with the Republic.

23:16.471 --> 23:19.908
- They've knocked out
all our communications.
- Do you have transports?

23:20.009 --> 23:22.409
In the main hangar.
This way.

23:27.017 --> 23:30.111
- There are too many of them.
- That won't be a problem.

23:30.220 --> 23:33.781
Your Highness, under the circumstances,
I suggest you come to Coruscant with us.

23:33.890 --> 23:36.985
Thank you, Ambassador,
but my place is with my people.

23:37.095 --> 23:39.757
- They will kill you if you stay.
- They wouldn't dare.

23:39.864 --> 23:43.631
They need her to sign a treaty
to make this invasion legal.
They can't afford to kill her.

23:43.735 --> 23:45.862
There is something else behind all this,
Your Highness.

23:45.971 --> 23:47.939
There's no logic
in the Federation's move here.

23:48.040 --> 23:50.032
My feelings tell me
they will destroy you.

23:50.143 --> 23:52.543
Our only hope is for
the senate to side with us.

23:52.645 --> 23:55.136
Senator Palpatine
will need your help.

23:55.248 --> 23:59.208
Either choice presents
great danger... to us all.

23:59.353 --> 24:01.253
We are brave,
Your Highness.

24:01.355 --> 24:04.620
If you are to leave,
Your Highness, it must be now.

24:04.725 --> 24:07.194
Then I will plead our case
to the senate.

24:07.295 --> 24:10.025
Be careful, Governor.

24:18.941 --> 24:22.139
We'll need to free
those pilots.

24:22.246 --> 24:24.146
I'll deal with that.

24:27.651 --> 24:30.120
- Halt!
- I'm ambassador to
the supreme chancellor.

24:30.221 --> 24:32.189
I'm taking these people
to Coruscant.

24:32.323 --> 24:35.554
- Where are you taking them?
- To Coruscant.

24:35.660 --> 24:38.289
Coruscant?
Uh, that doesn't compute.

24:38.397 --> 24:40.331
Uh, wait.
You're under arrest.

24:45.739 --> 24:48.037
Come on. Move!

24:52.346 --> 24:54.974
Go!

25:18.876 --> 25:22.175
Now, stay here
and keep out of trouble.

25:25.951 --> 25:29.079
- Hello, boyos.
- [Beeping, Whistling]

25:34.493 --> 25:36.085
There's the blockade.

25:44.972 --> 25:48.204
- [Alarm Beeping]
- The shield generator's been hit!

25:48.309 --> 25:51.244
[Alarm Blaring]

25:51.346 --> 25:53.576
[Beeping]

25:53.681 --> 25:56.549
[Gasps]

25:56.652 --> 25:58.244
How wude!

25:58.354 --> 26:01.983
[Whistling]

26:08.298 --> 26:09.890
We're losing droids fast.

26:10.033 --> 26:13.333
If we can't get the shield generator
fixed, we'll be sitting ducks.

26:15.506 --> 26:19.603
- The shields are gone.
- [Whistling, Beeping]

26:23.448 --> 26:26.179
The power's back!

26:26.286 --> 26:28.880
[Beeping]

26:28.988 --> 26:32.480
That little droid did it.
He bypassed the main power drive.

26:32.592 --> 26:35.153
Deflector shields up
at maximum.

26:44.773 --> 26:48.504
There's not enough power to get us
to Coruscant. The hyperdrive is leaking.

26:48.610 --> 26:51.512
We'll have to land somewhere
to refuel and repair the ship.

26:51.614 --> 26:53.809
Here, Master.
Tatooine.

26:53.916 --> 26:57.478
Small, out of the way, poor. The Trade
Federation have no presence there.

26:57.587 --> 26:59.452
How can you
be sure?

26:59.556 --> 27:01.490
It's controlled
by the Hutts.

27:01.591 --> 27:04.424
You can't take Her Royal Highness there.
The Hutts are gangsters.

27:04.528 --> 27:06.827
- If they discovered her...
- It'd be no different
than if we landed...

27:06.931 --> 27:08.831
on a system controlled
by the Federation,

27:08.933 --> 27:13.268
except that the Hutts aren't looking
for her, which gives us the advantage.

27:17.776 --> 27:20.769
And Queen Amidala,
has she signed the treaty?

27:20.914 --> 27:24.543
She has disappeared,
my lord.

27:24.651 --> 27:28.850
One Naboo cruiser
got past the blockade.

27:28.956 --> 27:31.891
[Snarls]
I want that treaty signed.

27:31.992 --> 27:34.017
My lord,

27:34.128 --> 27:36.723
it's impossible
to locate the ship.

27:36.832 --> 27:39.027
It's out of our range.

27:39.134 --> 27:41.898
Not for a Sith.

27:42.003 --> 27:43.904
This is my apprentice,

27:44.006 --> 27:45.906
Darth Maul.

27:47.243 --> 27:50.542
He will find
your lost ship.

27:54.918 --> 27:57.216
This is getting
out of hand.

27:57.321 --> 27:59.381
Now there are two of them.

27:59.491 --> 28:02.517
We should not
have made this bargain.

28:07.767 --> 28:11.328
An extremely well-put-together
little droid, Your Highness.

28:11.437 --> 28:14.338
Without a doubt, it saved the ship,
as well as our lives.

28:14.440 --> 28:17.774
It is to be commended.
What is its number?

28:17.878 --> 28:20.346
[Chirping, Beeping]

28:20.447 --> 28:22.575
R2-D2, Your Highness.

28:22.717 --> 28:27.814
- Thank you, R2-D2.
- [Happy Chirping]

28:27.955 --> 28:30.789
Padme.

28:30.893 --> 28:33.054
Clean this droid up
as best you can.

28:33.162 --> 28:35.130
It deserves our gratitude.

28:35.230 --> 28:36.788
[Whistling]

28:36.899 --> 28:39.425
Continue, Captain.

28:40.537 --> 28:42.937
Your Highness,
with your permission,

28:43.039 --> 28:46.100
we're heading for a remote planet
called Tatooine.

28:46.210 --> 28:49.577
It's in a system far beyond the reach
of the Trade Federation.

28:49.680 --> 28:52.308
I do not agree
with the Jedi on this.

28:52.416 --> 28:55.318
You must trust my judgment,
Your Highness.

28:56.755 --> 28:58.655
[Beeping]

28:58.757 --> 29:00.486
[JarJar]
Hello.

29:00.592 --> 29:03.562
Sorry.
Husa are yousa?

29:03.696 --> 29:06.164
I'm Padme.

29:06.265 --> 29:09.292
Mesa JarJar Binks.

29:09.403 --> 29:11.428
You're a Gungan,
aren't you?

29:11.538 --> 29:13.563
Uh-huh.

29:13.674 --> 29:17.270
- How'd you end up here with us?
- My no know.

29:17.378 --> 29:21.075
Mesa day starten pitty okeyday
witda brisky morning munchen.

29:21.182 --> 29:23.980
Den boom!
Getten berry scared...

29:24.085 --> 29:27.487
and grabben dat Jedi,
and pow... mesa here.

29:27.623 --> 29:30.285
- [Chirps]
- Huh. Mesa getten berry, berry scared.

29:30.426 --> 29:33.089
[Beeping]

29:37.000 --> 29:40.698
- That's it... Tatooine.
- There's a settlement.

29:40.805 --> 29:44.901
Land near the outskirts.
We don't want to attract attention.

30:02.195 --> 30:04.960
The hyperdrive generator's gone, Master.
We'll need a new one.

30:05.099 --> 30:07.567
That'll complicate things.
Be wary.

30:07.701 --> 30:10.829
- I sense a disturbance in the Force.
- I feel it also, Master.

30:10.938 --> 30:13.772
Don't let them send
any transmissions.

30:19.047 --> 30:21.482
This sun doen murder
to mesa skin.

30:21.584 --> 30:24.075
[Captain]
Wait!

30:24.186 --> 30:26.086
Wait.

30:29.026 --> 30:31.893
Her Highness commands you
to take her handmaiden with you.

30:31.995 --> 30:35.830
No more commands from
Her Highness today, Captain.

30:35.967 --> 30:38.026
The spaceport is not
going to be pleasant.

30:38.169 --> 30:40.262
The queen wishes it.

30:40.405 --> 30:42.339
She's curious
about the planet.

30:43.442 --> 30:45.967
[Sighs]
This is not a good idea.

30:46.078 --> 30:47.978
Stay close to me.

30:49.448 --> 30:52.316
[Chirps, Beeping]

31:01.762 --> 31:04.595
Moisture farms,
for the most part.

31:05.866 --> 31:09.598
Some indigenous tribes
and scavengers.

31:09.738 --> 31:14.073
The few spaceports like this one
are havens for those
that don't wish to be found.

31:14.177 --> 31:16.077
Like us.

31:17.413 --> 31:20.007
Dissen berry
berry bad.

31:20.116 --> 31:23.314
- [Sloshing Sound]
- Oh! Icky icky goo!

31:23.420 --> 31:26.287
[Chattering]

31:31.196 --> 31:33.357
[Creature Snorts]

31:36.301 --> 31:39.533
We'll try one
of the smaller dealers.

31:42.375 --> 31:44.366
[Bell Dinging]

31:44.510 --> 31:47.844
[Speaking Huttese]
Good day to you.

31:47.948 --> 31:49.711
What do you want?

31:49.816 --> 31:52.546
I need parts for a J-type 327 Nubian.

31:52.653 --> 31:56.715
Ah, yes! Nubian.
We have lots of that.

31:56.824 --> 31:59.292
Boy, get in here now!

31:59.394 --> 32:03.627
- My droid has a readout of what I need.
- [Grunting]

32:03.732 --> 32:05.632
[Speaking Huttese]
What took you so long?

32:05.734 --> 32:07.998
I was cleaning the fan switches.

32:08.103 --> 32:10.334
Watch the store.
I've got some selling to do.

32:10.440 --> 32:14.103
So... let me take thee
out back, huh?

32:14.244 --> 32:18.113
Ni you'll find what you need.
[Chuckling]

32:18.215 --> 32:20.581
- Hmm?
- Don't touch anything.

32:20.685 --> 32:22.585
Hmph!

32:27.859 --> 32:29.759
Hmm.

32:29.861 --> 32:33.559
- Are you an angel?
- What?

32:33.666 --> 32:37.397
An angel. I heard the deep space
pilots talk about them.

32:37.503 --> 32:40.405
They're the most beautiful
creatures in the universe.

32:40.507 --> 32:43.067
They live on the moons
of lego, I think.

32:43.177 --> 32:45.543
You're a funny little boy.

32:45.646 --> 32:47.547
How do you know so much?

32:47.649 --> 32:51.551
I listen to all the traders
and star pilots who come through here.

32:51.653 --> 32:55.988
I'm a pilot, you know, and someday
I'm gonna fly away from this place.

32:56.092 --> 33:00.051
- You're a pilot?
- Mm-hmm. All my life.

33:00.162 --> 33:02.494
How long have you
been here?

33:02.598 --> 33:06.558
Since I was very little.
Three, I think.

33:06.670 --> 33:09.400
My mom and I were sold
to Gardulla the Hutt,

33:09.506 --> 33:12.237
but she lost us betting
on the Podraces.

33:12.343 --> 33:14.174
You're a slave?

33:14.278 --> 33:18.443
- I'm a person, and my name is Anakin.
- I'm sorry.

33:18.550 --> 33:22.281
I don't fully understand.
This is a strange place to me.

33:22.421 --> 33:25.117
Hmm. Hmm.

33:25.257 --> 33:28.694
Where... Wheres
yousa goin?

33:28.795 --> 33:31.127
- Ugh!
- [Laughing]

33:31.231 --> 33:33.165
[JarJar Grunting]

33:33.266 --> 33:36.293
- [Blubbering] I got ya.
- Hey!

33:36.403 --> 33:38.166
- What?
- Hit the nose.

33:38.272 --> 33:40.763
Oh! Uh.

33:42.811 --> 33:46.372
A T-1 4 hyperdrive generator.
Thee in luck.

33:46.481 --> 33:49.109
I'm the only one
hereabouts who has one.

33:49.217 --> 33:52.745
But thee might as well buy a new ship.
It would be cheaper, huh?

33:52.855 --> 33:55.790
[Chuckles]
Saying of which,

33:55.925 --> 33:58.326
how's thee gonna pay
for all this, huh?

33:58.428 --> 34:00.487
I have 20,000
Republic dataries.

34:00.631 --> 34:02.462
Republic credits?

34:02.566 --> 34:05.536
Republic credits are no good out here.
I need something more real.

34:05.637 --> 34:08.765
I don't have anything else,
but credits will do fine.

34:08.873 --> 34:12.502
- No, they won't.
- Credits will do fine.

34:12.610 --> 34:14.442
No, they won't!

34:14.547 --> 34:18.745
What, you think you're some kind of
Jedi, waving your hand around like that?

34:18.851 --> 34:23.118
I'm a Toydarian. Mind tricks
don't work on me. Only money.

34:23.223 --> 34:27.353
- No money, no parts, no deal.
- [Beeping]

34:27.460 --> 34:31.989
And no one else has a T-14 hyperdrive,
I promise you that.

34:32.133 --> 34:34.033
[Grunts]

34:38.907 --> 34:42.638
Wouldn't have lasted long anyways if
I wasn't so good at building things.

34:42.744 --> 34:45.305
Oh! Aw! Ooh! Uh!

34:45.415 --> 34:48.907
- Ai, ai! Whoa, ai!
- We're leaving. JarJar.

34:49.018 --> 34:51.282
- Whaaa!
-[Metal Clanging, Crashing]

34:51.387 --> 34:53.948
I'm glad to have
met you, Anakin.

34:54.058 --> 34:55.889
I was glad to meet you too.

34:58.028 --> 35:01.021
What? Wha... Oh.

35:02.534 --> 35:04.434
[Groaning]

35:04.536 --> 35:08.871
[Speaking In Huttese]
Outlanders. They think we know nothing.

35:08.975 --> 35:10.909
They seemed nice to me.

35:11.010 --> 35:12.944
Clean the racks.

35:13.045 --> 35:14.273
Then you can go home.

35:14.380 --> 35:16.315
Yippee!

35:17.451 --> 35:19.316
[Sighs]

35:22.322 --> 35:24.757
[Qui-Gon] And you're sure
there's nothing left on board?

35:24.859 --> 35:26.759
A few containers of supplies.

35:26.861 --> 35:29.921
The queen's wardrobe, maybe,
but not enough for you to barter with,

35:30.031 --> 35:32.364
not in the amount
you're talking about.

35:32.468 --> 35:34.902
All right. I'm sure another solution
will present itself.

35:35.037 --> 35:36.937
I'll check back later.

35:37.039 --> 35:39.406
Noah gain!
Noah gain.

35:39.509 --> 35:42.376
Da beings hereabouts,
cawazy!

35:42.479 --> 35:44.947
Wesa be wobbed
un crunched!

35:45.081 --> 35:48.245
Not likely. We have nothing of value.
That's our problem.

35:48.352 --> 35:51.480
[Whistling]

35:56.628 --> 36:00.064
Hmm?
Ah, mooie-mooie.

36:01.466 --> 36:04.903
Hey, hey! [Speaking Huttese]
Are you going to pay for that?

36:05.004 --> 36:06.801
Huh? Wanga?

36:06.906 --> 36:08.771
It costs seven wupiupi.

36:11.946 --> 36:13.971
Ah! Chubaa...

36:14.114 --> 36:16.446
Oops.
[Whistling]

36:16.550 --> 36:18.018
[Growling]

36:19.421 --> 36:21.912
[Speaking Huttese]
Is this yours?

36:22.023 --> 36:23.684
Who, mesa? [Gags]

36:23.792 --> 36:25.658
[Alien Speaking In Huttese]

36:25.728 --> 36:27.719
Ouch! Ouch!

36:27.830 --> 36:29.957
[Speaking Huttese]
Careful, Sebulba.

36:30.066 --> 36:32.227
He's a big-time outlander.

36:32.335 --> 36:35.772
I'd hate to see you diced
before we race again.

36:35.872 --> 36:39.035
Next time we race, boy,
it will be the end of you.

36:39.142 --> 36:42.943
If you weren't a slave,
I'd squash you now.

36:43.081 --> 36:46.073
Yeah, it'd be a pity
if you had to pay for me.

36:47.618 --> 36:50.782
- Hi.
- Hi there.

36:50.889 --> 36:53.722
Your buddy here was about
to be turned into orange goo.

36:53.826 --> 36:57.319
He picked a fight with a Dug, an
especially dangerous Dug called Sebulba.

36:57.430 --> 37:01.025
Mesa haten crunchen.
Das da las ting mesa want.

37:01.134 --> 37:05.128
Nevertheless, the boy is right.
You were heading into trouble.

37:05.239 --> 37:07.139
Thanks, my young friend.

37:07.241 --> 37:09.300
But... But...

37:09.410 --> 37:12.744
- But mesa doen nutten!
- [Growls]

37:14.249 --> 37:17.514
[Wind Whistling]

37:19.856 --> 37:22.416
This storm
will slow them down.

37:22.558 --> 37:25.288
- Looks pretty bad.
- [Beeps]

37:25.395 --> 37:27.956
- Panaka.
- [Man] Receiving a message from home.

37:28.065 --> 37:30.260
- We'll be right there.
- [Beeps]

37:36.207 --> 37:38.368
[Anakin]
Here, you'll like these pallies.

37:38.476 --> 37:41.070
- Here.
- Thank you.

37:42.247 --> 37:44.546
Oh, my bones are aching.

37:44.650 --> 37:49.212
Storm's coming up, Ani.
You better get home quick.

37:49.355 --> 37:52.223
- Do you have shelter?
- We'll head back to our ship.

37:52.325 --> 37:54.919
- Is it far?
- It's on the outskirts.

37:55.062 --> 37:57.462
You'll never reach
the outskirts in time.

37:57.564 --> 38:01.433
Sandstorms are very,
very dangerous.

38:01.536 --> 38:04.027
Come on.
I'll take you to my place.

38:04.138 --> 38:06.471
[Whistling, Beeping]

38:17.520 --> 38:19.920
[Exhaling]
Mom!

38:20.023 --> 38:23.755
- Mom, I'm home!
-[JarJar] Ahh, dissen cozy.

38:23.894 --> 38:26.294
- These are my friends, Mom.
- [JarJar] Hello.

38:26.397 --> 38:29.925
- I'm Qui-Gon J inn.
- I'm building a droid. You wanna see?

38:30.068 --> 38:32.468
Your son was kind enough
to offer us shelter.

38:32.571 --> 38:36.029
- Come on. I'll show you 3PO.
- Oh, mooie-mooie.

38:36.141 --> 38:39.077
[Beeping, Chirping]

38:43.716 --> 38:46.982
Isn't he great?
He's not finished yet.

38:47.087 --> 38:48.987
He's wonderful.

38:49.089 --> 38:51.956
- [Beeping]
-[Anakin] You really like him?

38:52.059 --> 38:54.995
He's a protocol droid
to help Mom. Watch.

38:56.498 --> 39:00.764
Oh. Oh. Uh...
Where is everybody?

39:00.869 --> 39:04.169
Whoops. Yeah.

39:04.273 --> 39:06.434
Oh, hello.

39:06.542 --> 39:09.876
I am C-3 PO,
human-cyborg relations.

39:09.980 --> 39:11.880
How might I serve you?

39:11.982 --> 39:14.746
- He's perfect.
- Oh. Perfect.

39:14.851 --> 39:18.413
When the storm is over, I'll show you
my racer. I'm building a Podracer.

39:18.523 --> 39:22.357
- [Whistling]
- I'm not sure this floor
is entirely stable.

39:22.460 --> 39:25.658
Oh, hello. I don't believe we
have been introduced.

39:25.764 --> 39:27.459
[Excited Beeping]

39:27.566 --> 39:29.830
R2-D2.
A pleasure to meet you.

39:29.968 --> 39:32.995
I am C-3PO,
human-cyborg relations.

39:33.139 --> 39:35.573
[Chirping, Bleeping]

39:35.675 --> 39:38.872
I beg your pardon,
but what do you mean, " naked"?

39:40.548 --> 39:43.813
My parts are showing?
My goodness! Oh!

39:48.390 --> 39:50.858
The death toll
is catastrophic.

39:50.959 --> 39:53.359
We must bow
to their wishes.

39:53.461 --> 39:55.521
You must contact me.

39:55.631 --> 39:58.327
It's a trick.
Send no reply.

39:58.434 --> 40:01.961
Send no transmissions
of any kind.

40:02.104 --> 40:05.632
It sounds like bait
to establish a connection trace.

40:05.776 --> 40:09.712
What if it is true,
and the people are dying?

40:09.846 --> 40:12.315
Either way,
we're running out of time.

40:25.931 --> 40:28.093
Tatooine is
sparsely populated.

40:28.201 --> 40:30.999
If the trace was correct,
I will find them quickly, Master.

40:31.104 --> 40:33.004
Move against
the Jedi first.

40:33.106 --> 40:35.837
You will then have no difficulty
in taking the queen to Naboo...

40:35.977 --> 40:37.877
to sign the treaty.

40:37.979 --> 40:40.140
At last we will reveal
ourselves to the Jedi.

40:40.281 --> 40:42.716
At last we will
have revenge.

40:42.818 --> 40:45.719
You have been well-trained,
my young apprentice.

40:45.821 --> 40:48.221
They will be
no match for you.

40:53.062 --> 40:58.023
All slaves have a transmitter
placed inside their bodies somewhere.

40:58.135 --> 41:01.161
I've been working on a scanner
to try and locate mine.

41:01.272 --> 41:04.764
- Any attempt to escape...
- And they blow you up!

41:04.875 --> 41:07.310
- Boom!
- How wude!

41:07.412 --> 41:09.846
I can't believe there's
still slavery in the galaxy.

41:09.981 --> 41:11.881
The Republic's
antislavery laws...

41:11.983 --> 41:14.316
The Republic
doesn't exist out here.

41:14.420 --> 41:17.446
We must survive
on our own.

41:17.590 --> 41:20.218
[Gulps]
Xcuse me.

41:20.326 --> 41:23.763
Has anybody ever seen
a Podrace?

41:23.864 --> 41:28.460
They have Podracing on Malastare.
Very fast, very dangerous.

41:28.568 --> 41:31.129
I'm the only human
who can do it.

41:31.239 --> 41:34.402
You must have Jedi reflexes
if you race pods.

41:34.509 --> 41:36.774
- [Gasps]
- Don't do that again.

41:36.879 --> 41:40.645
[Yelping, Blubbering]

41:42.251 --> 41:44.812
You're a Jedi knight,
aren't you?

41:46.890 --> 41:49.358
What makes you think that?

41:49.459 --> 41:53.726
I saw your laser sword.
Only Jedis carry that kind of weapon.

41:53.831 --> 41:56.732
Perhaps I killed a Jedi
and took it from him.

41:56.834 --> 41:58.734
I don't think so.

41:58.803 --> 42:00.965
No one can kill a Jedi.

42:01.073 --> 42:03.871
I wish that were so.

42:03.975 --> 42:06.034
I had a dream
I was a Jedi.

42:06.144 --> 42:09.308
I came back here
and freed all the slaves.

42:09.415 --> 42:12.782
- Have you come to free us?
- No, I'm afraid not.

42:12.885 --> 42:17.220
I think you have.
Why else would you be here?

42:22.129 --> 42:24.894
I can see there's
no fooling you, Anakin.

42:24.999 --> 42:28.025
We're on our way to Coruscant,
the central system in the Republic,

42:28.136 --> 42:30.161
on a very important mission.

42:30.271 --> 42:33.298
How did you end up out here
in the outer rim?

42:33.409 --> 42:37.038
Our ship was damaged, and we're stranded
here until we can repair it.

42:37.146 --> 42:39.274
I can help.

42:39.383 --> 42:43.149
- I can fix anything.
-[Qui-Gon] I believe you can.

42:43.253 --> 42:46.086
But first we must acquire
the parts we need.

42:46.189 --> 42:48.920
Wit no-nutten mula
to trade.

42:49.060 --> 42:52.552
These junk dealers must have
a weakness of some kind.

42:52.697 --> 42:57.135
Gambling. Everything here revolves
around betting on those awful races.

42:57.269 --> 43:01.467
Podracing.
Greed can be a powerful ally.

43:01.573 --> 43:04.441
I built a racer.
It's the fastest ever.

43:04.544 --> 43:07.035
There's a big race tomorrow
on Boonta Eve.

43:07.147 --> 43:09.741
- You could enter my pod.
-[Mother] Anakin!

43:09.849 --> 43:12.910
- Watto won't let you.
- Watto doesn't know I've built it.

43:13.020 --> 43:14.920
You could make him think
it was yours...

43:15.022 --> 43:17.286
and get him to let me
pilot it for you.

43:17.391 --> 43:21.590
I don't want you to race. It's awful.
I die every time Watto makes you do it.

43:21.730 --> 43:23.857
But, Mom, I love it.

43:23.999 --> 43:27.527
The prize money would more than pay
for the parts they need.

43:27.670 --> 43:29.968
Anakin.

43:30.072 --> 43:32.870
Your mother's right.

43:32.975 --> 43:36.070
Is there anyone friendly to the Republic
who can help us?

43:37.381 --> 43:39.246
No.

43:44.289 --> 43:48.919
Mom, you say the biggest problem in this
universe is nobody helps each other.

43:52.932 --> 43:56.663
I'm sure Qui-Gon doesn't want
to put your son in danger.

43:56.802 --> 43:58.703
We'll find some other way.

43:58.805 --> 44:01.069
No.

44:01.174 --> 44:03.642
There is no other way.

44:03.743 --> 44:08.113
I may not like it,
but he can help you.

44:08.216 --> 44:10.776
He was meant
to help you.

44:18.427 --> 44:20.362
[Growling]

44:24.367 --> 44:26.267
Are you sure about this?

44:26.369 --> 44:29.032
Trusting our fate
to a boy we hardly know?

44:29.173 --> 44:31.164
The queen
will not approve.

44:31.308 --> 44:34.243
The queen
doesn't need to know.

44:34.345 --> 44:35.938
Well, I don't approve.

44:36.081 --> 44:39.744
-[Bell Dings]
- The boy tells me you want to
sponsor him in the race.

44:39.851 --> 44:44.880
How can you do this? Not on
the Republic credits, I think, huh?

44:44.991 --> 44:47.152
My ship will be
the entry fee.

44:47.260 --> 44:49.353
Oh, not bad!

44:49.462 --> 44:52.455
Not bad, huh?
A Nubian, huh?

44:52.566 --> 44:55.865
It's in good order,
except for the parts I need.

44:55.969 --> 44:58.494
What would the boy ride?

44:58.605 --> 45:02.167
He smashed up my pod in the last race.
It will take some long time to fix it.

45:02.310 --> 45:06.406
It wasn't my fault, really.
Sebulba flashed me with his vents.

45:06.548 --> 45:09.916
I actually saved the pod,
mostly.

45:10.019 --> 45:13.477
Mmm. That you did, huh.
[Chuckling]

45:13.622 --> 45:16.456
The boy's good.
No doubts there, huh?

45:16.560 --> 45:20.860
I have acquired a pod in a game
of chance, the fastest ever built.

45:20.964 --> 45:26.096
I hope you didn't kill
anyone I know for it, huh?

45:26.203 --> 45:27.966
[Laughing]

45:28.072 --> 45:31.133
So, you supply the pod
and the entry fee,

45:31.243 --> 45:33.143
and I supply the boy.

45:33.245 --> 45:37.147
We split the winnings,
um, 50-50, I think, huh?

45:37.282 --> 45:41.879
If it's going to be 50-50, I suggest
you front the cash for the entry.

45:42.021 --> 45:44.046
If we win,

45:44.190 --> 45:47.991
you keep all the winnings,
minus the cost of the parts I need.

45:48.095 --> 45:51.326
And if we lose,
you keep my ship.

45:52.633 --> 45:55.159
Either way, you win.

45:55.270 --> 45:56.965
[Grumbling]

45:57.072 --> 45:59.563
[Grumbling Continues]

46:00.976 --> 46:03.309
Deal!

46:07.483 --> 46:12.183
[Speaking Huttese]
Your friend is a foolish one, methinks.

46:19.731 --> 46:22.666
What if this plan fails,
Master?

46:22.767 --> 46:25.532
We could be stuck here
a very long time.

46:25.638 --> 46:28.129
Well, it's too dangerous
to call for help,

46:28.240 --> 46:31.676
and a ship without a power supply
isn't going to get us anywhere.

46:31.777 --> 46:33.746
And...

46:33.847 --> 46:36.680
there's something
about this boy.

46:41.856 --> 46:44.882
You should be very proud
of your son.

46:45.026 --> 46:48.018
He gives without
any thought of reward.

46:48.163 --> 46:51.030
Well, he knows
nothing of greed.

46:51.133 --> 46:55.069
- He has a...
- He has special powers.

46:56.239 --> 46:58.139
Yes.

46:58.241 --> 47:00.835
He can see things
before they happen.

47:00.943 --> 47:03.777
That's why he appears
to have such quick reflexes.

47:03.881 --> 47:05.781
It's a Jedi trait.

47:05.883 --> 47:08.716
-He deserves better than a slave's life.
- Why, certainly.

47:08.819 --> 47:12.187
Had he been born in the Republic,
we would have identified him early.

47:12.290 --> 47:17.193
The Force is unusually strong with him.
That much is clear.

47:18.363 --> 47:20.264
Who was his father?

47:22.968 --> 47:24.902
There was no father.

47:26.338 --> 47:29.706
I carried him, I gave birth,
I raised him.

47:29.810 --> 47:33.041
I can't explain
what happened.

47:34.715 --> 47:36.513
Can you help him?

47:36.617 --> 47:38.517
I don't know.

47:41.022 --> 47:44.618
I didn't actually
come here to free slaves.

47:48.864 --> 47:51.766
[Giggling]

47:51.868 --> 47:53.768
Hey, hi, Ani.

47:53.870 --> 47:56.395
Hi.

47:56.539 --> 47:59.703
-[R2-D 2 Beeping]
- Wow, a real astro droid.

47:59.810 --> 48:01.471
[Beeping]

48:01.579 --> 48:05.379
- How did you get so lucky?
- That isn't the half of it.

48:05.483 --> 48:08.419
- I'm in the Boonta race tomorrow.
- What?

48:08.520 --> 48:10.249
With this?

48:10.355 --> 48:13.153
[Speaking Alien Language]
You're such a joker, Ani.

48:13.258 --> 48:16.490
- You've been working on
that thing for years.
- It's never gonna run.

48:16.596 --> 48:18.791
Come on.
Let's go and play ball.

48:18.898 --> 48:22.164
Keep racing, Ani.
You're gonna be bug squash.

48:22.302 --> 48:24.702
[All Giggling]

48:28.742 --> 48:30.643
Hey, JarJar.

48:30.745 --> 48:33.145
- [Gasps]
- Keep away from those energy binders.

48:33.248 --> 48:36.706
If your hand gets caught in the beam,
it's gonna go numb for hours.

48:36.818 --> 48:38.844
Sorry. Okay.

48:38.954 --> 48:42.185
[Yelping, Blubbering]

48:42.291 --> 48:44.452
[Muffled]
My tongue is fat.

48:44.560 --> 48:47.689
My tongue...
Wrench.

48:47.798 --> 48:50.460
Where is da wrench?
Oh, dare it is.

48:50.567 --> 48:53.162
Hey. Uh-oh.

48:53.271 --> 48:56.468
Uh, Ani, I'm stuck.
Ani...

48:56.607 --> 49:00.601
You know, I find that JarJar creature
to be a little odd.

49:00.746 --> 49:02.338
[Gurgling]

49:02.481 --> 49:05.314
You don't even know
if this thing's gonna run.

49:05.417 --> 49:07.510
- It will.
- I think it's time we found out.

49:07.619 --> 49:09.850
- Here, use this power charge.
- Yes, sir!

49:09.956 --> 49:12.049
Come on, Kitster.
Let's move away.

49:12.158 --> 49:14.319
[Muffled]
My... My mouth.

49:14.427 --> 49:18.023
Ani, I'm stuck.
[Babbling]

49:19.667 --> 49:23.194
Uh, hey.
My tongue is fat. Ani!

49:23.304 --> 49:26.240
You're quite right.
He's very odd indeed.

49:27.342 --> 49:30.038
Oh. Th... Thank you.

49:30.178 --> 49:32.079
Go.

49:32.181 --> 49:34.775
[Engine Humming]

49:46.563 --> 49:50.193
It's working!
It's working!

50:00.813 --> 50:03.339
Stay still, Ani.
Let me clean this cut.

50:03.483 --> 50:07.419
There's so many.
Do they all have a system of planets?

50:07.554 --> 50:09.419
Most of them.

50:09.522 --> 50:11.491
Has anyone been
to 'em all?

50:11.626 --> 50:14.424
[Chuckles]
Not likely.

50:14.528 --> 50:17.588
I wanna be the first one
to see 'em all.

50:18.934 --> 50:21.334
-[Mother] Ani, bedtime!
- Ow!

50:21.436 --> 50:24.200
There we are.
Good as new.

50:24.306 --> 50:27.208
Ani, I'm not gonna
tell you again.

50:27.310 --> 50:30.768
- What are you doing?
- Checking your blood for infections.

50:30.880 --> 50:34.510
Go on. You have
a big day tomorrow.

50:34.618 --> 50:36.518
Sleep well, Ani.

50:39.290 --> 50:41.258
- Obi-Wan?
- Yes, Master?

50:41.392 --> 50:42.121
I need an analysis of this blood sample
I'm sending you.

50:43.595 --> 50:46.928
- Wait a minute.
- [Beeping]

50:47.032 --> 50:49.000
I need
a midi-chlorian count.

50:51.938 --> 50:54.566
The reading
is off the chart.

50:54.707 --> 50:56.572
Over 20,000.

50:56.709 --> 51:00.305
Even Master Yoda doesn't have
a midi-chlorian count that high.

51:00.447 --> 51:02.278
No Jedi has.

51:02.382 --> 51:04.441
What does that mean?

51:04.551 --> 51:06.452
I'm not sure.

51:51.504 --> 51:55.236
[Rhythmic Tones Sounding,
Whirring]

52:08.057 --> 52:11.493
- [Jabbering]
-[Creature Trumpeting]

52:16.867 --> 52:19.802
I wanna see your spaceship
the moment the race is over.

52:19.903 --> 52:23.635
Patience, my blue friend. You'll have
your winnings before the suns set.

52:23.741 --> 52:25.971
And we'll be far away
from here.

52:26.077 --> 52:29.638
Not if your ship belongs
to me, I think, huh?

52:29.747 --> 52:33.616
[Laughs]
I warn you, no funny business.

52:33.719 --> 52:36.847
- You don't think Anakin can win?
- Don't get me wrong, no.

52:36.989 --> 52:39.458
I have great faith
in the boy.

52:39.592 --> 52:41.685
He's a credit
to your race,

52:41.828 --> 52:45.059
but, uh, Sebulba there
is going to win, I think.

52:45.165 --> 52:47.066
[Laughing]

52:47.168 --> 52:48.931
Oh, no!

52:50.271 --> 52:52.967
[Speaking Huttese]

52:53.074 --> 52:54.940
Why do you think that?

52:55.043 --> 52:58.843
He always wins!
[Laughing]

52:58.947 --> 53:01.381
I am betting heavily
on Sebulba.

53:03.219 --> 53:06.552
- I'll take that bet.
- You what?

53:06.656 --> 53:10.024
I'll wager my new racing pod
against, say,

53:10.160 --> 53:12.060
the boy and his mother.

53:12.162 --> 53:15.859
No pod is worth two slaves,
not by a long shot.

53:15.966 --> 53:18.527
The boy, then.

53:18.636 --> 53:21.332
Hmm. Well, uh...

53:24.742 --> 53:27.268
We'll let fate decide,
huh?

53:27.379 --> 53:30.815
I just happen to have
a chance cube here.

53:30.916 --> 53:33.977
Blue, it's the boy.

53:34.087 --> 53:38.285
Red, uh... his mother.

53:46.134 --> 53:47.863
[Grumbling]

53:47.969 --> 53:52.669
You won this small toss, outlander,
but you won't win the race!

53:52.774 --> 53:54.867
So it makes
little difference!

53:58.681 --> 54:01.616
[Creature Groaning]

54:01.718 --> 54:04.586
[Watto Speaking Huttese]

54:04.688 --> 54:07.282
Better stop your friend's betting,

54:07.391 --> 54:10.986
or I'll end up owning him too.

54:11.095 --> 54:13.223
[Chuckling]

54:13.331 --> 54:15.822
- What'd he mean by that?
- I'll tell you later.

54:15.967 --> 54:17.992
Good morning.

54:18.136 --> 54:20.105
-[Bleeping]
- Oh, my.

54:20.239 --> 54:22.207
Space travel sounds
rather perilous.

54:22.341 --> 54:24.206
[Beeping]

54:24.310 --> 54:28.338
I can assure you, they will never get
me onto one of those dreadful starships.

54:28.448 --> 54:31.849
This is so wizard, Ani.
I'm sure you'll do it this time.

54:31.952 --> 54:36.219
- Do what?
- Finish the race, of course.

54:36.324 --> 54:40.920
- You've never won a race?
- Well, not exactly.

54:41.029 --> 54:43.054
Not even finished?

54:43.165 --> 54:45.656
Kitster's right.
I will this time.

54:45.768 --> 54:47.759
Of course you will.

54:53.877 --> 54:55.970
[Whirring]

55:04.288 --> 55:07.781
[Crowd Cheering]

55:11.663 --> 55:15.122
[Announcer Speaking
In Huttese]

55:15.235 --> 55:17.328
[Continues]
...Podracers.

55:17.437 --> 55:19.302
That's absolutely right.

55:19.405 --> 55:24.434
And a big turnout here from all corners
of the outer rim territories.

55:24.578 --> 55:28.173
I see the contestants are making
their way out onto the starting grid.

55:28.315 --> 55:30.216
[Announcer
Speaking In Huttese]

55:30.318 --> 55:33.151
[Announcer
from the Tund System.

55:33.255 --> 55:36.156
[Announcer

55:38.828 --> 55:41.296
[Announcer
Two-time winner Boles Roor.

55:41.397 --> 55:43.695
[Speaking Huttese]

55:43.799 --> 55:46.462
Sebulba!

55:46.570 --> 55:49.471
[Crowd Cheering]

55:52.709 --> 55:55.907
[Speaking I n Huttese]

55:56.047 --> 55:59.107
And in the front row,
nearside pole position,

55:59.250 --> 56:01.242
Mawhonic!

56:02.488 --> 56:04.479
- [Shouts]
-A hearty hello...

56:04.623 --> 56:08.354
to Clegg Holdfast
and his Voltec KT9 Wasp!

56:08.460 --> 56:11.225
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

56:11.331 --> 56:14.357
And back again,
it's the mighty Dud Bolt...

56:14.467 --> 56:19.064
with that incredible racing machine,
the Vulptereen 3 2 7.

56:22.410 --> 56:24.709
-And hoping for a big win today,
- [Jabbering]

56:24.813 --> 56:29.216
Ody Mandrell, with his
record-setting pit droid team.

56:29.351 --> 56:31.444
[Bleeping]

56:31.586 --> 56:34.021
[Tool Whirring]

56:34.123 --> 56:37.388
And a late entry,
young Anakin Skywalker,

56:37.493 --> 56:39.985
- A local boy.
- [Cheering]

56:41.498 --> 56:43.762
I see the flags are moving
out onto the track.

56:53.845 --> 56:56.280
-[Flatulence]
- Huh? [Sniffs]

56:56.382 --> 56:58.782
[Snorting]

56:58.884 --> 57:00.875
[Blubbering]
Pee yousa!

57:03.623 --> 57:05.523
Be safe.

57:05.625 --> 57:09.026
I will, Mom.
I promise.

57:18.639 --> 57:21.370
Uh-oh.
[Snickering]

57:24.079 --> 57:26.878
[Speaking I n Huttese]
You won't walk away from this one,

57:26.983 --> 57:29.247
you slave scum.

57:29.352 --> 57:32.583
Don't count on it, slime ball.

57:32.689 --> 57:34.851
You're bantha fodder!

57:34.959 --> 57:37.052
[Chuckling, Muttering]

57:39.130 --> 57:41.860
- You all set, Ani?
- Yep.

57:41.966 --> 57:43.867
- Right.
- Whoa!

57:47.339 --> 57:50.366
Remember, concentrate
on the moment.

57:50.476 --> 57:54.242
Feel, don't think.
Use your instincts.

57:54.347 --> 57:56.008
I will.

57:56.115 --> 57:58.311
May the Force
be with you.

58:02.122 --> 58:04.022
[Fanfare]

58:04.124 --> 58:07.151
[Speaking I n Huttese]

58:07.262 --> 58:10.254
Jabba the Hutt.
[Ululating]

58:10.398 --> 58:12.593
[Spectators Cheering]

58:12.734 --> 58:15.203
Mmm.
[Muttering I n Huttese]

58:19.308 --> 58:23.006
[Speaking Huttese]
Welcome.

58:25.048 --> 58:28.142
Begin the race!

58:35.693 --> 58:38.595
[Announcer
Speaking In Huttese]

58:38.697 --> 58:41.825
[Announcer
they're clearing the grid.

58:43.068 --> 58:44.969
- Is he nervous?
- He's fine.

58:46.573 --> 58:49.474
You Jedi are far too reckless.
The queen is not...

58:49.576 --> 58:52.478
The queen trusts my judgment,
young handmaiden.

58:52.580 --> 58:54.480
You should too.

58:54.582 --> 58:57.016
You assume too much.

58:57.117 --> 59:00.178
[Announcer
Start your engines.

59:39.466 --> 59:42.833
Oh, dissen gonna be messy.
Me no watch'n!

59:52.847 --> 59:54.713
Oh!

59:54.816 --> 59:57.182
[Squeaks]

59:57.286 --> 59:59.481
- [Clang]
- [Beep]

01:00:02.825 --> 01:00:05.487
Oh, no! No!

01:00:05.595 --> 01:00:08.325
[Engine Clicking,
Winding Down]

01:00:09.766 --> 01:00:13.066
[Chuckles]
Wait. Little Skywalker has stalled.

01:00:13.170 --> 01:00:16.071
- [Cursing I n Alien Language]
- [All Laughing]

01:00:23.515 --> 01:00:27.748
[Announcer
Well, it looks like Quadinaros
is having engine trouble also.

01:00:29.322 --> 01:00:31.790
- Come on, Ani!
- [Engine Clicking, Whirring]

01:00:37.064 --> 01:00:40.227
-[Announcer
-And there goes Skywalker!
- Go, Ani, go!

01:00:40.334 --> 01:00:42.462
He will be hard-pressed
to catch up with the leaders.

01:00:44.539 --> 01:00:48.236
- Ehh!
- [Cursing I n Huttese]

01:00:54.350 --> 01:00:56.580
Haaaa!

01:01:51.080 --> 01:01:52.981
[Speaking I n Tusken Dialect]

01:01:56.119 --> 01:02:00.887
Looks like a few Tusken Raiders
are camped out on the canyon dune turn.

01:02:02.060 --> 01:02:04.153
[Shouting]

01:02:07.833 --> 01:02:10.825
Doowat macroon!

01:02:13.172 --> 01:02:16.870
Ooh, there goes
Quadinaros' power coupling.

01:02:18.578 --> 01:02:20.478
Cheespa will be!

01:02:20.580 --> 01:02:22.172
Ooh!

01:02:22.282 --> 01:02:26.185
-[Announcer
Chubba ni chees Sebulba!
- Packet!

01:02:26.287 --> 01:02:27.982
Kulkah doka!

01:02:28.222 --> 01:02:32.717
- [Beep]
-[Announcer
Ody Mandrell coona of wound!

01:02:32.828 --> 01:02:35.695
[Fussing I n Alien Language]

01:02:37.332 --> 01:02:39.460
[Squeaking]

01:02:39.602 --> 01:02:41.069
Whoa!

01:02:42.371 --> 01:02:44.498
[Laughing]

01:02:44.607 --> 01:02:46.838
Oh, no!

01:02:46.944 --> 01:02:49.742
- Oh.
- [Screaming]

01:02:51.615 --> 01:02:54.710
- Where is Master Anakin?
- [Beeping]

01:02:56.721 --> 01:02:58.951
Look.
Here he comes.

01:03:01.292 --> 01:03:04.194
[Announcer
is moving up in the field.

01:03:04.296 --> 01:03:06.423
Yay!
Yippee!

01:03:08.467 --> 01:03:10.868
[Talking I n Alien Language]

01:03:12.539 --> 01:03:15.508
- [Beeping]
- He has to complete two more circuits?

01:03:15.642 --> 01:03:17.543
Oh, dear.

01:04:08.202 --> 01:04:09.794
Ah.

01:04:09.903 --> 01:04:12.236
[Grunts]
He has!

01:04:14.742 --> 01:04:17.677
Arrr!

01:04:25.154 --> 01:04:27.019
Skywalker's spinning
out of control!

01:04:27.123 --> 01:04:28.681
[Gasps]

01:05:24.988 --> 01:05:28.924
Oh, I don't care what universe
you're from. That's gotta hurt!

01:05:35.967 --> 01:05:37.731
Here he comes!
Money!

01:05:37.836 --> 01:05:40.964
[Announcer
the final lap, Sebulba's in the lead,

01:05:41.073 --> 01:05:43.564
followed closely by Skywalker!

01:05:43.676 --> 01:05:46.646
Go, Ani!

01:06:10.006 --> 01:06:13.942
-[Spectators Gasping]
- Skywalker's been forced
onto the service ramp!

01:06:16.580 --> 01:06:18.241
[Engine Winding Down]

01:06:18.349 --> 01:06:21.011
Whoa-oa!

01:06:30.962 --> 01:06:32.726
- Huh?
- [Engine Starts]

01:06:35.634 --> 01:06:39.297
- It's Skywalker!
- Sebulba!

01:06:39.405 --> 01:06:43.706
Amazing! A quick control thrust,
and he's back on course!

01:06:43.810 --> 01:06:45.539
Did he crash-ed?

01:06:50.051 --> 01:06:52.349
- [Chattering]
- Wah hota!

01:07:08.405 --> 01:07:10.339
[Beeping]

01:07:20.519 --> 01:07:21.918
[Laughing]

01:07:26.526 --> 01:07:29.723
Skywalker's in trouble!
Sebulba takes the lead!

01:07:29.829 --> 01:07:31.660
[Spectators Continue Cheering]

01:08:22.722 --> 01:08:25.418
- He's catching Sebulba!
- Inkabunga!

01:08:25.525 --> 01:08:28.050
Careful, Ani.
Careful, Ani!

01:08:29.396 --> 01:08:31.489
Wha...
Chuba da noya!

01:08:46.549 --> 01:08:48.141
[Spectators Cheering]

01:08:58.395 --> 01:09:01.797
- That little human being
is out of his mind.
- Punda tah punda!

01:09:01.900 --> 01:09:04.460
- They're side by side!
- Bangu du bangu!

01:09:11.744 --> 01:09:13.735
Wa-waaaaah!

01:09:21.288 --> 01:09:23.189
Aaah!

01:09:24.425 --> 01:09:26.325
Poo doo!

01:09:26.427 --> 01:09:28.657
[Cheering]

01:09:31.733 --> 01:09:33.633
- Yippee!
- Yay!

01:09:33.735 --> 01:09:36.329
Ya eeka buta!
Whoo-hoo-hoo!

01:09:36.438 --> 01:09:39.567
- [Beeping]
- I can't believe it.

01:09:39.676 --> 01:09:41.576
The crowds
are going nuts!

01:09:41.678 --> 01:09:43.805
Oh! Ah!
Oh! Ah!

01:09:45.982 --> 01:09:50.352
[Chanting]
Ooh! Ah! Ooh! Ah! Ooh! Ah! Ooh! Ah!

01:09:50.487 --> 01:09:52.512
[JarJar]
Yay, Ani!

01:09:53.891 --> 01:09:56.884
Mom, I did it!
Yeah!

01:09:57.028 --> 01:10:00.327
[Arguing]

01:10:00.432 --> 01:10:02.333
[Snoring]

01:10:02.435 --> 01:10:04.335
[Muttering, Speaking Huttese]

01:10:04.437 --> 01:10:06.337
Ohh!

01:10:07.440 --> 01:10:09.340
[JarJar]
Good going, Ani!

01:10:09.442 --> 01:10:12.037
[Chanting Continues, Faint]

01:10:13.680 --> 01:10:15.671
We owe you everything,
Ani.

01:10:15.782 --> 01:10:18.183
- Mmm!
- Aww.

01:10:18.286 --> 01:10:20.379
It's so wonderful,
Ani.

01:10:20.488 --> 01:10:23.218
You have brought hope
to those who have none.

01:10:23.358 --> 01:10:25.554
I'm so very proud
of you.

01:10:25.694 --> 01:10:27.594
[Creature Bellows]

01:10:27.696 --> 01:10:29.596
Aww.

01:10:29.698 --> 01:10:32.098
Oy chuba no.

01:10:33.837 --> 01:10:35.930
[Sighs]

01:10:36.039 --> 01:10:37.939
You.

01:10:38.041 --> 01:10:40.373
You swindled me!

01:10:40.477 --> 01:10:44.312
You knew the boy was going to win.
Somehow you knew it.

01:10:44.415 --> 01:10:46.315
I lost everything.

01:10:46.417 --> 01:10:49.319
Whenever you gamble, my friend,
eventually you'll lose.

01:10:49.421 --> 01:10:52.288
Bring the parts
to the main hangar.

01:10:52.391 --> 01:10:55.724
I'll come by your shop later on
so you can release the boy.

01:10:55.861 --> 01:10:59.127
You can't have him.
It wasn't a fair bet.

01:11:01.934 --> 01:11:04.836
- Would you like to discuss
it with the Hutts?
-[Grumbles]

01:11:04.938 --> 01:11:06.997
I'm sure
they can settle this.

01:11:09.510 --> 01:11:11.410
Take him.

01:11:18.353 --> 01:11:20.254
[JarJar]
Hidoe!

01:11:20.356 --> 01:11:23.257
Well, we have all
the essential parts we need.

01:11:23.359 --> 01:11:26.453
I'm going back. Some unfinished
business. I won't be long.

01:11:26.562 --> 01:11:30.055
Why do I sense we've picked up
another pathetic life-form?

01:11:30.200 --> 01:11:34.034
It's the boy who's responsible
for getting us these parts.

01:11:34.137 --> 01:11:36.038
Get this hyperdrive
generator installed.

01:11:36.140 --> 01:11:38.700
Yes, Master.
That shouldn't take long.

01:11:38.810 --> 01:11:40.971
- Come on. Hup!
-[Creature Grunts]

01:11:45.584 --> 01:11:48.712
Hey.
These are yours.

01:11:48.821 --> 01:11:50.721
Yes!

01:11:52.258 --> 01:11:54.158
Mom, we sold the pod!

01:11:54.260 --> 01:11:56.660
- Look at all the money we have!
- My goodness!

01:11:56.763 --> 01:11:59.631
- But that's so wonderful, Ani.
-And he has been freed.

01:11:59.734 --> 01:12:02.498
- What?
- You're no longer a slave.

01:12:04.438 --> 01:12:06.372
Did you hear that?

01:12:06.475 --> 01:12:09.638
Now you can make
your dreams come true, Ani.

01:12:09.745 --> 01:12:12.407
You are free.

01:12:15.585 --> 01:12:17.485
Will you take him
with you?

01:12:17.587 --> 01:12:19.885
- Is he to become a Jedi?
- Yes.

01:12:19.989 --> 01:12:21.889
Our meeting
was not a coincidence.

01:12:21.991 --> 01:12:24.426
Nothing happens
by accident.

01:12:24.528 --> 01:12:28.089
You mean I get to come with you
in your starship?

01:12:28.198 --> 01:12:30.099
Anakin,

01:12:31.503 --> 01:12:34.802
training to become a Jedi
is not an easy challenge,

01:12:34.906 --> 01:12:37.842
and even if you succeed,
it's a hard life.

01:12:37.943 --> 01:12:41.071
But I wanna go.
It's what I've always dreamed of doing.

01:12:41.213 --> 01:12:44.080
Can I go, Mom?

01:12:44.183 --> 01:12:46.414
Anakin,

01:12:46.520 --> 01:12:49.751
this path has been placed
before you.

01:12:49.856 --> 01:12:52.347
The choice
is yours alone.

01:12:55.997 --> 01:12:57.897
I wanna do it.

01:12:59.467 --> 01:13:01.698
Then pack your things.
We haven't much time.

01:13:01.804 --> 01:13:03.863
Yippee!

01:13:08.978 --> 01:13:10.878
What about Mom?

01:13:14.017 --> 01:13:15.917
Is she free too?

01:13:16.019 --> 01:13:19.547
I tried to free your mother, Ani,
but Watto wouldn't have it.

01:13:19.657 --> 01:13:22.558
You're coming with us,
aren't you, Mom?

01:13:30.202 --> 01:13:33.900
Son, my place is here.
My future is here.

01:13:34.006 --> 01:13:37.407
It is time
for you to let go.

01:13:37.510 --> 01:13:39.637
I don't want things
to change.

01:13:39.745 --> 01:13:42.146
But you can't stop
the change...

01:13:42.282 --> 01:13:45.308
any more than you can
stop the suns from setting.

01:13:46.453 --> 01:13:48.354
Oh, I love you.

01:13:49.791 --> 01:13:51.691
[Sighs]

01:13:54.028 --> 01:13:55.929
Now hurry.

01:14:00.970 --> 01:14:02.870
Thank you.

01:14:02.972 --> 01:14:05.874
I'll watch after him.
You have my word.

01:14:07.878 --> 01:14:10.540
Will you be all right?

01:14:10.647 --> 01:14:12.513
Yeah.

01:14:14.752 --> 01:14:17.186
Oh!
Oh, my. Oh!

01:14:17.321 --> 01:14:19.222
Hello, Master Anakin.

01:14:19.324 --> 01:14:21.383
Well, 3 PO,
I've been freed...

01:14:21.527 --> 01:14:23.927
and I'm going away
in a starship.

01:14:24.029 --> 01:14:26.965
Master Anakin, you are my maker
and I wish you well.

01:14:27.066 --> 01:14:31.298
However, I should prefer it if
I were a little more completed.

01:14:31.404 --> 01:14:36.741
I'm sorry I wasn't able to finish you,
3 PO, give you coverings and all.

01:14:36.844 --> 01:14:40.803
I'm gonna miss working on you.
You've been a great pal.

01:14:40.915 --> 01:14:43.817
I'll make sure Mom doesn't
sell you or anything.

01:14:43.919 --> 01:14:45.648
Sell me?

01:14:45.754 --> 01:14:47.346
Bye.

01:14:47.455 --> 01:14:49.355
Oh, my.

01:15:12.850 --> 01:15:15.752
I can't do it, Mom.
I just can't do it.

01:15:15.854 --> 01:15:18.516
Ani.

01:15:19.825 --> 01:15:22.021
Will I ever
see you again?

01:15:23.496 --> 01:15:26.397
What does your heart
tell you?

01:15:27.734 --> 01:15:29.965
I hope so.

01:15:30.071 --> 01:15:31.971
Yes.

01:15:32.073 --> 01:15:33.973
I guess.

01:15:34.075 --> 01:15:36.977
Then we will
see each other again.

01:15:40.015 --> 01:15:42.916
I will come back
and free you, Mom.

01:15:43.018 --> 01:15:44.953
I promise.

01:15:52.830 --> 01:15:56.129
Now, be brave...

01:15:56.266 --> 01:15:58.928
and don't look back.

01:15:59.069 --> 01:16:00.970
Don't look back.

01:16:23.865 --> 01:16:25.765
[Probe Speaks
I n Droid Language]

01:16:46.222 --> 01:16:49.192
- Qui-Gon, sir, wait! I'm tired!
- Anakin! Drop!

01:16:51.662 --> 01:16:54.564
Go!
Tell them to take off!

01:17:08.181 --> 01:17:10.081
Qui-Gon's
in trouble.

01:17:10.184 --> 01:17:11.879
Take off.

01:17:12.986 --> 01:17:14.749
Over there.
Fly low.

01:17:35.679 --> 01:17:37.579
Are you all right?

01:17:37.714 --> 01:17:39.614
I think so.

01:17:39.716 --> 01:17:41.617
What was it?

01:17:41.719 --> 01:17:45.120
I'm not sure, but it was
well-trained in the Jedi arts.

01:17:45.223 --> 01:17:48.215
- [Beeps]
- My guess is it was after the queen.

01:17:48.326 --> 01:17:50.852
What are we gonna do
about it?

01:17:50.963 --> 01:17:52.692
[Sighs]

01:17:52.798 --> 01:17:54.698
We shall be patient.

01:17:54.800 --> 01:17:57.599
Anakin Skywalker,
meet Obi-Wan Kenobi.

01:17:57.704 --> 01:17:59.899
- Hi.
-[R2-D 2 Beeping]

01:18:00.006 --> 01:18:03.703
You're a Jedi too?
Pleased to meet you.

01:18:10.918 --> 01:18:13.820
Your queen is lost,
your people are starving,

01:18:13.922 --> 01:18:15.822
and you, Governor,
are going to die...

01:18:15.924 --> 01:18:18.825
much sooner than your people,
I'm afraid.

01:18:18.927 --> 01:18:21.089
This invasion
will gain you nothing.

01:18:21.197 --> 01:18:24.223
We're a democracy.
The people have decided.

01:18:24.333 --> 01:18:26.233
Take him away.

01:18:29.673 --> 01:18:32.574
My troops are in position
to begin searching the swamps...

01:18:32.676 --> 01:18:35.076
for these rumored
underwater villages.

01:18:35.179 --> 01:18:37.580
They will not
stay hidden for long.

01:18:41.753 --> 01:18:44.154
[Muttering, Snoring]

01:18:48.627 --> 01:18:51.358
The death toll
is catastrophic.

01:18:51.464 --> 01:18:54.092
We must bow
to their wishes.

01:18:54.201 --> 01:18:56.431
You must
contact me.

01:19:10.552 --> 01:19:12.486
You all right?

01:19:12.588 --> 01:19:15.217
It's very cold.

01:19:16.659 --> 01:19:19.560
[Continues Muttering, Snoring]

01:19:23.267 --> 01:19:26.168
You come from
a warm planet, Ani.

01:19:26.270 --> 01:19:28.670
A little too warm
for my taste.

01:19:28.772 --> 01:19:31.037
Space is cold.

01:19:31.142 --> 01:19:33.303
You seem sad.

01:19:34.446 --> 01:19:36.744
The queen is worried.

01:19:36.848 --> 01:19:39.283
Her people are suffering,
dying.

01:19:39.385 --> 01:19:42.877
She must convince the senate
to intervene, or...

01:19:44.357 --> 01:19:46.622
I'm not sure what'll happen.

01:19:48.061 --> 01:19:50.120
I made this for you...

01:19:51.632 --> 01:19:53.532
so you'd remember me.

01:19:53.635 --> 01:19:56.934
I carved it
out of a japor snippet.

01:19:57.038 --> 01:19:59.871
It'll bring you
good fortune.

01:19:59.974 --> 01:20:01.875
It's beautiful.

01:20:01.977 --> 01:20:05.378
But I don't need this
to remember you by.

01:20:08.017 --> 01:20:11.419
Many things will change
when we reach the capital, Ani,

01:20:11.521 --> 01:20:14.081
but my caring for you
will remain.

01:20:16.793 --> 01:20:19.922
I care for you, too,
only l...

01:20:20.031 --> 01:20:22.192
Miss your mother.

01:20:40.688 --> 01:20:44.886
Coruscant.
The entire planet is one big city.

01:20:44.992 --> 01:20:46.755
There's Chancellor Valorum's shuttle.

01:20:46.860 --> 01:20:50.126
And look over there.
Senator Palpatine is waiting for us.

01:21:19.431 --> 01:21:22.662
It is a great gift to see you alive,
Your Majesty.

01:21:22.768 --> 01:21:25.601
With the communications breakdown,
we've been very concerned.

01:21:25.704 --> 01:21:28.333
I'm anxious to hear your report
on the situation.

01:21:28.441 --> 01:21:31.069
May I present
Supreme Chancellor Valorum.

01:21:31.211 --> 01:21:35.308
Welcome, Your Highness. It's an honor
to finally meet you in person.

01:21:35.449 --> 01:21:38.009
Thank you,
Supreme Chancellor.

01:21:38.152 --> 01:21:41.315
I must relay to you how distressed
everyone is over the current situation.

01:21:41.422 --> 01:21:45.154
I've called for a special session
of the senate to hear your position.

01:21:45.260 --> 01:21:48.161
I'm grateful for your concern,
Chancellor.

01:21:48.263 --> 01:21:50.163
There is a question
of procedure,

01:21:50.265 --> 01:21:52.996
but I'm confident
we can overcome it.

01:21:53.102 --> 01:21:56.003
I must speak with
the Jedi Council immediately.

01:21:56.105 --> 01:21:58.904
The situation has become
much more complicated.

01:22:04.681 --> 01:22:06.582
Ani, come on.

01:22:17.129 --> 01:22:20.530
The queen's a bein' grossly nice,
mesa tinks.

01:22:21.868 --> 01:22:23.836
Pitty hot.

01:22:48.398 --> 01:22:51.595
[Men Conversing, Faint]

01:22:51.701 --> 01:22:56.036
[Palpatine]
There is no civility, only politics.

01:22:56.140 --> 01:23:00.042
The Republic
is not what it once was.

01:23:00.144 --> 01:23:05.412
The senate is full of greedy,
squabbling delegates.

01:23:05.517 --> 01:23:07.382
There is no interest...

01:23:07.486 --> 01:23:09.580
in the common good.

01:23:09.689 --> 01:23:11.919
I must be frank,
Your Majesty.

01:23:12.058 --> 01:23:14.959
There is little chance the senate
will act on the invasion.

01:23:15.061 --> 01:23:17.963
Chancellor Valorum
seems to think there is hope.

01:23:18.065 --> 01:23:22.161
If I may say so, Your Majesty,
the chancellor has little real power.

01:23:22.269 --> 01:23:26.172
He is mired by baseless
accusations of corruption.

01:23:26.274 --> 01:23:30.005
- The bureaucrats are in charge now.
- What options have we?

01:23:30.111 --> 01:23:33.673
Our best choice would be
to push for the election...

01:23:33.782 --> 01:23:35.682
of a stronger
supreme chancellor,

01:23:35.784 --> 01:23:38.275
one who could control
the bureaucrats...

01:23:38.387 --> 01:23:40.219
and give us justice.

01:23:40.323 --> 01:23:44.589
You could call for
a vote of no confidence...

01:23:44.728 --> 01:23:46.628
in Chancellor Valorum.

01:23:46.730 --> 01:23:49.222
He has been
our strongest supporter.

01:23:49.367 --> 01:23:54.600
Our only other choice would be
to submit a plea to the courts.

01:23:54.705 --> 01:23:58.039
The courts take even longer
to decide things than the senate.

01:23:58.143 --> 01:24:01.044
Our people are dying,
Senator.

01:24:01.146 --> 01:24:04.878
We must do something quickly
to stop the Federation.

01:24:04.984 --> 01:24:07.612
To be realistic,
Your Majesty,

01:24:07.720 --> 01:24:12.681
I think we're going to have to accept
Federation control for the time being.

01:24:14.461 --> 01:24:16.520
That is something
I cannot do.

01:24:23.905 --> 01:24:26.500
He was trained
in the Jedi arts.

01:24:26.609 --> 01:24:30.545
My only conclusion can be
that it was a Sith lord.

01:24:30.646 --> 01:24:34.845
I mpossible. The Sith have been
extinct for a millennium.

01:24:34.952 --> 01:24:39.150
I do not believe the Sith
could have returned without us knowing.

01:24:39.256 --> 01:24:42.351
Ah, hard to see,
the dark side is.

01:24:42.460 --> 01:24:45.361
We will use all our resources
to unravel this mystery.

01:24:45.463 --> 01:24:48.455
We will discover the identity
of your attacker.

01:24:48.566 --> 01:24:50.467
May the Force
be with you.

01:24:54.073 --> 01:24:56.007
[Yoda]
Master Qui-Gon.

01:24:56.108 --> 01:24:58.509
More to say have you?

01:25:00.780 --> 01:25:02.680
With your permission,
my master,

01:25:04.184 --> 01:25:07.211
I have encountered
a vergence in the Force.

01:25:08.322 --> 01:25:10.347
A vergence, you say?

01:25:10.458 --> 01:25:12.585
Located around a person?

01:25:12.693 --> 01:25:14.594
A boy.

01:25:14.696 --> 01:25:18.530
His cells have the highest
concentration of midi-chlorians
I have seen in a life-form.

01:25:18.634 --> 01:25:21.502
It is possible he was conceived
by the midi-chlorians.

01:25:23.172 --> 01:25:25.538
You refer
to the prophecy...

01:25:25.675 --> 01:25:28.075
of the one who will bring
balance to the Force.

01:25:28.177 --> 01:25:30.043
You believe
it's this boy?

01:25:30.147 --> 01:25:32.741
- I don't presume to...
-[Yoda] But you do.

01:25:32.850 --> 01:25:35.478
Revealed your opinion is.

01:25:35.586 --> 01:25:37.612
I request the boy
be tested, Master.

01:25:37.722 --> 01:25:42.955
Oh? Trained as a Jedi
you request for him, hmm?

01:25:43.061 --> 01:25:45.826
Finding him
was the will of the Force.

01:25:45.931 --> 01:25:47.831
I have no doubt of that.

01:25:51.537 --> 01:25:53.904
[Sighs]

01:25:54.007 --> 01:25:56.532
Bring him before us, then.

01:26:06.654 --> 01:26:09.556
- [Beeps]
- The boy's here to see Padme.

01:26:09.658 --> 01:26:11.558
[Woman]
Let him in.

01:26:14.463 --> 01:26:18.366
I'm sorry, Ani,
but Padme's not here right now.

01:26:18.468 --> 01:26:20.800
Who is it?

01:26:20.904 --> 01:26:23.931
Anakin Skywalker to see Padme,
Your Highness.

01:26:24.041 --> 01:26:25.941
I've sent Padme
on an errand.

01:26:26.043 --> 01:26:30.913
I'm on my way to the Jedi temple
to start my training, I hope.

01:26:31.049 --> 01:26:34.883
I may never see her again,
so I came to say good-bye.

01:26:34.986 --> 01:26:36.886
We will tell her for you.

01:26:36.988 --> 01:26:39.617
We are sure
her heart goes with you.

01:26:39.726 --> 01:26:41.785
Thank you, Your Highness.

01:26:55.777 --> 01:26:59.838
The chair recognizes the senator
from the sovereign system of Naboo.

01:26:59.948 --> 01:27:03.009
[Senators Murmuring]

01:27:06.655 --> 01:27:11.059
[Palpatine] Supreme Chancellor,
delegates of the senate,

01:27:11.161 --> 01:27:13.561
a tragedy has occurred...

01:27:13.663 --> 01:27:17.190
which started right here
with the taxation of trade routes...

01:27:17.300 --> 01:27:20.327
and has now engulfed
our entire planet...

01:27:20.438 --> 01:27:22.429
in the oppression
of the Trade Federation.

01:27:22.540 --> 01:27:24.770
This is outrageous!

01:27:24.876 --> 01:27:27.437
I object to
the senator's statements.

01:27:27.546 --> 01:27:31.607
The chair does not recognize the senator
from the Trade Federation at this time.

01:27:31.717 --> 01:27:35.586
To state our allegations,
I present Queen Amidala,

01:27:35.688 --> 01:27:37.679
recently elected
ruler of the Naboo,

01:27:37.824 --> 01:27:39.724
who speaks
on our behalf.

01:27:39.826 --> 01:27:41.727
[Murmuring Continues]

01:27:45.733 --> 01:27:48.463
Honorable representatives
of the Republic,

01:27:48.569 --> 01:27:51.698
I come to you under
the gravest of circumstances.

01:27:51.807 --> 01:27:54.799
The Naboo system has been invaded
by the droid armies of the Trade...

01:27:54.910 --> 01:27:58.369
I object!
There is no proof!

01:27:58.481 --> 01:28:00.381
This is incredible.

01:28:00.483 --> 01:28:04.545
We recommend a commission be sent
to Naboo to ascertain the truth.

01:28:04.655 --> 01:28:06.850
The Congress of Malastare concurs...

01:28:06.957 --> 01:28:09.755
with the honorable delegate
from the Trade Federation.

01:28:09.860 --> 01:28:12.261
- A commission must be appointed.
- The point...

01:28:12.397 --> 01:28:15.525
- Excuse me, Chancellor.
-[Palpatine] Enter the bureaucrat.

01:28:15.667 --> 01:28:18.329
The true rulers
of the Republic.

01:28:18.436 --> 01:28:22.601
And on the payroll of
the Trade Federation, I might add.

01:28:22.708 --> 01:28:26.940
This is where Chancellor Valorum's
strength will disappear.

01:28:28.515 --> 01:28:30.847
[Valorum]
The point is conceded.

01:28:30.951 --> 01:28:33.852
Will you defer your motion
to allow a commission...

01:28:33.954 --> 01:28:36.480
to explore the validity
of your accusations?

01:28:36.591 --> 01:28:38.491
I will not defer.

01:28:38.593 --> 01:28:42.085
I've come before you to resolve
this attack on our sovereignty now.

01:28:42.196 --> 01:28:45.223
I was not elected to watch
my people suffer and die...

01:28:45.367 --> 01:28:47.995
while you discuss this invasion
in a committee.

01:28:50.305 --> 01:28:53.366
If this body
is not capable of action,

01:28:53.476 --> 01:28:56.502
I suggest new leadership
is needed.

01:28:58.248 --> 01:29:01.150
I move for a vote
of no confidence...

01:29:01.252 --> 01:29:03.243
in Chancellor Valorum's
leadership.

01:29:03.354 --> 01:29:06.722
[Senators Murmuring,
Shouting]

01:29:10.328 --> 01:29:12.489
Vote now!
Vote now!

01:29:12.597 --> 01:29:15.362
Vote now!
Vote now!

01:29:15.468 --> 01:29:18.198
- [Chanting Continues]
Vote now! Vote now!
- Order!

01:29:18.337 --> 01:29:21.238
Now they will elect
a new chancellor,

01:29:21.340 --> 01:29:23.241
a strong chancellor,

01:29:23.343 --> 01:29:26.244
one who will not let
our tragedy continue.

01:29:27.948 --> 01:29:32.249
The boy will not pass the council's
test, Master. He's too old.

01:29:32.353 --> 01:29:35.322
Anakin will become a Jedi,
I promise you.

01:29:35.423 --> 01:29:38.325
Do not defy the council,
Master, not again.

01:29:38.427 --> 01:29:41.157
I shall do what I must,
Obi-Wan.

01:29:43.065 --> 01:29:46.797
If you would just follow the code,
you would be on the council.

01:29:46.903 --> 01:29:50.031
They will not go along
with you this time.

01:29:50.140 --> 01:29:53.075
You still have much to learn,
my young apprentice.

01:29:56.380 --> 01:29:59.281
A ship.

01:29:59.383 --> 01:30:01.352
A cup.

01:30:01.453 --> 01:30:03.250
A ship.

01:30:04.356 --> 01:30:06.847
A speeder.

01:30:08.861 --> 01:30:10.761
Hmm.

01:30:13.399 --> 01:30:15.299
How feel you?

01:30:15.401 --> 01:30:17.302
Cold, sir.

01:30:18.539 --> 01:30:20.404
Afraid are you?

01:30:20.507 --> 01:30:22.441
No, sir.

01:30:22.543 --> 01:30:25.172
See through you we can.

01:30:25.313 --> 01:30:27.213
Be mindful
of your feelings.

01:30:27.315 --> 01:30:30.079
Your thoughts dwell
on your mother.

01:30:31.753 --> 01:30:34.245
- I miss her.
-[Yoda] Mmm.

01:30:34.390 --> 01:30:36.881
Afraid to lose her,
I think, mmm?

01:30:36.993 --> 01:30:39.154
What has that got to do
with anything?

01:30:39.261 --> 01:30:41.594
Everything.

01:30:41.698 --> 01:30:44.758
Fear is the path
to the dark side.

01:30:44.868 --> 01:30:47.770
Fear leads to anger.
Anger leads to hate.

01:30:47.872 --> 01:30:51.239
Hate leads to suffering.

01:30:57.783 --> 01:31:00.684
I sense much fear in you.

01:31:13.601 --> 01:31:17.002
Yousa tinking
yousa people ganna die?

01:31:17.104 --> 01:31:19.005
I don't know.

01:31:19.107 --> 01:31:21.667
Gungans get pasted too, eh?

01:31:23.445 --> 01:31:26.141
I hope not.

01:31:26.248 --> 01:31:28.877
Gungans no dyin'
without a fight.

01:31:28.985 --> 01:31:30.885
Wesa warriors.

01:31:31.020 --> 01:31:34.422
Wesa got a grand army.

01:31:34.525 --> 01:31:37.926
Dat's why you no liken us,
mesa tinks.

01:31:38.028 --> 01:31:40.861
Your Highness?

01:31:42.032 --> 01:31:44.160
Your Highness.

01:31:44.269 --> 01:31:47.397
Senator Palpatine has been nominated
to succeed Valorum...

01:31:47.505 --> 01:31:49.564
as supreme chancellor.

01:31:49.674 --> 01:31:52.576
A surprise, to be sure,
but a welcome one.

01:31:52.678 --> 01:31:57.377
Your Majesty, if I am elected,
I promise to put an end to corruption.

01:31:57.483 --> 01:31:59.145
Who else
has been nominated?

01:31:59.252 --> 01:32:03.586
Bail Antilles of Alderaan
and Ainlee Teem of Malastare.

01:32:03.690 --> 01:32:08.628
I feel confident our situation will
create a strong sympathy vote for us.

01:32:10.364 --> 01:32:12.332
I will be chancellor.

01:32:12.467 --> 01:32:15.096
I fear by the time you have
control of the bureaucrats,

01:32:15.204 --> 01:32:18.435
there'll be nothing left of our people,
our way of life.

01:32:18.540 --> 01:32:20.440
I understand your concern,
Your Majesty.

01:32:20.542 --> 01:32:24.070
Unfortunately, the Federation
has possession of our planet.

01:32:25.849 --> 01:32:29.946
Senator,
this is your arena.

01:32:30.054 --> 01:32:31.954
I feel I must
return to mine.

01:32:34.592 --> 01:32:37.494
I've decided
to go back to Naboo.

01:32:37.629 --> 01:32:39.597
Go back?
But, Your Majesty, be realistic.

01:32:39.698 --> 01:32:41.598
They'll force you
to sign the treaty.

01:32:41.700 --> 01:32:44.100
I will sign no treaty,
Senator.

01:32:44.202 --> 01:32:46.694
My fate will be no different
than that of our people.

01:32:46.839 --> 01:32:48.739
- Captain.
- Your Highness.

01:32:48.841 --> 01:32:50.741
Ready my ship.

01:32:50.843 --> 01:32:54.541
Please, Your Majesty,
stay here where it's safe.

01:32:54.648 --> 01:32:57.811
It is clear to me now that
the Republic no longer functions.

01:32:57.918 --> 01:33:02.253
I pray you will bring sanity
and compassion back to the senate.

01:33:12.434 --> 01:33:14.994
The Force
is strong with him.

01:33:15.137 --> 01:33:17.038
He is to be trained,
then?

01:33:18.508 --> 01:33:21.568
No, he will not
be trained.

01:33:21.678 --> 01:33:23.339
No?

01:33:25.383 --> 01:33:27.442
He is too old.

01:33:27.552 --> 01:33:31.353
He is the chosen one.
You must see it.

01:33:31.456 --> 01:33:36.086
Mmm. Clouded
this boy's future is.

01:33:38.297 --> 01:33:40.095
I will train him, then.

01:33:44.470 --> 01:33:47.304
I take Anakin
as my Padawan learner.

01:33:47.408 --> 01:33:50.377
An apprentice you have,
Qui-Gon.

01:33:50.477 --> 01:33:52.843
I mpossible
to take on a second.

01:33:52.947 --> 01:33:54.643
The code forbids it.

01:33:54.749 --> 01:33:58.150
- Obi-Wan is ready.
- I am ready to face the trials.

01:33:58.253 --> 01:34:01.882
Our own counsel we will keep
on who is ready.

01:34:01.990 --> 01:34:03.891
He is headstrong,

01:34:03.993 --> 01:34:07.360
and he has much to learn of
the living Force, but he is capable.

01:34:07.463 --> 01:34:10.729
There is little more
he can learn from me.

01:34:12.069 --> 01:34:13.934
Young Skywalker's fate...

01:34:14.037 --> 01:34:15.868
will be decided later.

01:34:15.973 --> 01:34:18.534
Now is not the time
for this.

01:34:18.676 --> 01:34:21.304
The senate is voting
for a new supreme chancellor,

01:34:21.446 --> 01:34:24.108
and Queen Amidala
is returning home,

01:34:24.249 --> 01:34:27.481
which will put pressure
on the Federation and could
widen the confrontation.

01:34:27.586 --> 01:34:29.884
And draw out
the queen's attacker.

01:34:29.989 --> 01:34:34.393
Go with the queen to Naboo and discover
the identity of this dark warrior.

01:34:35.662 --> 01:34:37.562
This is the clue we need...

01:34:37.664 --> 01:34:39.928
to unravel
the mystery of the Sith.

01:34:40.033 --> 01:34:42.867
May the Force
be with you.

01:34:56.051 --> 01:34:58.953
It's not disrespect, Master.
It's the truth.

01:34:59.055 --> 01:35:00.955
From your point of view.

01:35:01.057 --> 01:35:04.458
The boy is dangerous.
They all sense it. Why can't you?

01:35:04.560 --> 01:35:07.462
His fate is uncertain.
He's not dangerous.

01:35:07.564 --> 01:35:09.964
The council will decide
Anakin's future.

01:35:10.067 --> 01:35:12.969
That should be enough for you.
Now get on board.

01:35:16.841 --> 01:35:18.741
[Whimpers]

01:35:18.843 --> 01:35:22.371
Qui-Gon, sir,
I don't want to be a problem.

01:35:22.481 --> 01:35:24.711
You won't be, Ani.

01:35:24.850 --> 01:35:28.912
I'm not allowed to train you, so I want
you to watch me and be mindful.

01:35:29.056 --> 01:35:31.957
Always remember:

01:35:32.059 --> 01:35:34.721
Your focus
determines your reality.

01:35:34.828 --> 01:35:37.992
Stay close to me
and you'll be safe.

01:35:38.099 --> 01:35:39.930
Master, sir,

01:35:40.034 --> 01:35:43.630
I heard Yoda talking
about midi-chlorians.

01:35:43.739 --> 01:35:47.266
I've been wondering...
What are midi-chlorians?

01:35:48.544 --> 01:35:50.944
Midi-chlorians are
a microscopic life-form...

01:35:51.046 --> 01:35:53.277
that resides
within all living cells.

01:35:54.718 --> 01:35:57.619
- They live inside me?
- I nside your cells, yes.

01:35:57.721 --> 01:36:01.214
- And we are symbionts with them.
- Symbionts?

01:36:01.359 --> 01:36:05.261
Life-forms living together
for mutual advantage.

01:36:05.363 --> 01:36:08.265
Without the midi-chlorians,
life could not exist...

01:36:08.367 --> 01:36:11.165
and we would have no
knowledge of the Force.

01:36:11.269 --> 01:36:13.169
They continually
speak to us,

01:36:13.271 --> 01:36:15.968
telling us
the will of the Force.

01:36:16.075 --> 01:36:18.202
When you learn
to quiet your mind,

01:36:18.311 --> 01:36:20.211
you'll hear them
speaking to you.

01:36:20.313 --> 01:36:22.213
I don't understand.

01:36:22.315 --> 01:36:25.808
With time and training, Ani,
you will. You will.

01:36:29.623 --> 01:36:33.890
Your Majesty, it is our pleasure
to continue to serve and protect you.

01:36:34.029 --> 01:36:35.929
I welcome your help.

01:36:36.031 --> 01:36:39.433
Senator Palpatine fears that
the Federation means to destroy me.

01:36:39.535 --> 01:36:42.698
I assure you I will not
allow that to happen.

01:36:42.805 --> 01:36:45.706
Wesa goin' ho-o-o-me!

01:36:45.808 --> 01:36:48.710
- Come on, R2.
- [Whistles]

01:36:57.288 --> 01:37:00.314
Is the planet secure?

01:37:00.425 --> 01:37:04.328
We have taken over the last pockets
of primitive life-forms.

01:37:04.463 --> 01:37:07.523
We are in complete control
of the planet now.

01:37:07.666 --> 01:37:13.537
Good. I will see to it that in
the senate things stay as they are.

01:37:13.640 --> 01:37:17.543
I am sending my apprentice,
Darth Maul, to join you.

01:37:17.645 --> 01:37:19.545
Yes, my lord.

01:37:19.647 --> 01:37:21.547
A Sith here?

01:37:26.955 --> 01:37:29.423
Those are
the forward stabilizers.

01:37:29.524 --> 01:37:31.924
And those two
control the pitch?

01:37:33.463 --> 01:37:35.363
You catch on
pretty quick.

01:37:35.465 --> 01:37:37.365
[Panaka]
As soon as we land,

01:37:37.467 --> 01:37:40.197
the Federation will arrest you
and force you to sign the treaty.

01:37:40.336 --> 01:37:44.068
I agree. I'm not sure what
you wish to accomplish by this.

01:37:44.174 --> 01:37:47.075
I will take back
what's ours.

01:37:47.177 --> 01:37:49.612
There are too few of us,
Your Highness.

01:37:49.714 --> 01:37:51.614
We have no army.

01:37:51.716 --> 01:37:55.277
And I can only protect you.
I can't fight a war for you.

01:37:55.386 --> 01:37:57.378
JarJar Binks.

01:37:57.490 --> 01:38:00.482
Mesa, Your Highness?

01:38:00.593 --> 01:38:03.494
Yes.
I need your help.

01:38:08.702 --> 01:38:10.932
I have one battleship
on my scope.

01:38:11.071 --> 01:38:13.131
[Obi-Wan]
It's a droid control ship.

01:38:13.274 --> 01:38:15.174
They've probably
spotted us.

01:38:15.276 --> 01:38:17.267
We haven't much time.

01:38:28.825 --> 01:38:32.727
- JarJar is on his way
to the Gungan city, Master.
- Good.

01:38:32.829 --> 01:38:35.731
Do you think the queen's idea
will work?

01:38:35.833 --> 01:38:38.734
The Gungans will not
be easily swayed.

01:38:38.836 --> 01:38:41.634
And we cannot use our power
to help her.

01:38:43.408 --> 01:38:46.536
I'm... I'm sorry for
my behavior, Master.

01:38:46.678 --> 01:38:50.341
It's not my place to disagree
with you about the boy.

01:38:52.318 --> 01:38:55.617
And I am grateful you think
I'm ready to take the trials.

01:38:56.756 --> 01:38:58.657
You've been a good apprentice,
Obi-Wan.

01:39:00.093 --> 01:39:02.994
And you're a much wiser man
than I am.

01:39:03.096 --> 01:39:06.863
I foresee you will become
a great Jedi knight.

01:39:09.737 --> 01:39:11.637
[Grunts]

01:39:12.907 --> 01:39:14.773
[Blubbering]

01:39:19.815 --> 01:39:22.216
Desa nobody dare.

01:39:22.319 --> 01:39:24.480
The Gungan city
is deserted.

01:39:24.621 --> 01:39:27.146
Some kinda fight,
mesa tinks.

01:39:27.290 --> 01:39:30.385
Do you think they have been
taken to the camps?

01:39:30.494 --> 01:39:32.860
More likely
they were wiped out.

01:39:32.964 --> 01:39:36.024
- Mesa no tink so.
- Do you know where they are, JarJar?

01:39:36.133 --> 01:39:39.570
When in trouble,
Gungans go to sacred place.

01:39:39.671 --> 01:39:42.572
Mesa show you.
Come on. Mesa show you!

01:39:46.279 --> 01:39:48.679
[Creatures Bleating]

01:40:00.127 --> 01:40:04.531
Your Honor,
Queen Amidala of the Naboo.

01:40:09.739 --> 01:40:14.540
Uh, h-heyo dadee,
Big Boss Nass, Your Honor.

01:40:14.644 --> 01:40:17.739
JarJar Binks.

01:40:17.848 --> 01:40:21.944
Who's da uss-en uthers?

01:40:22.052 --> 01:40:24.351
I am Queen Amidala
of the Naboo.

01:40:24.489 --> 01:40:27.583
I come before you
in peace.

01:40:27.725 --> 01:40:30.592
Ah, Naboo biggen.

01:40:30.695 --> 01:40:33.893
Yousa bringen
da Mackineeks.

01:40:33.999 --> 01:40:37.730
Yousa all bombad.

01:40:37.836 --> 01:40:41.432
We have searched you out because
we wish to form an alliance.

01:40:41.541 --> 01:40:43.441
Your Honor.

01:40:45.111 --> 01:40:48.081
Whosa dis?

01:40:48.182 --> 01:40:51.015
- I am Queen Amidala.
- Huh?

01:40:52.053 --> 01:40:53.918
This is my decoy,

01:40:54.021 --> 01:40:57.389
my protection,
my loyal bodyguard.

01:40:57.492 --> 01:41:01.792
I'm sorry for my deception,
but it was necessary to protect myself.

01:41:01.930 --> 01:41:04.832
Although we do not
always agree, Your Honor,

01:41:04.934 --> 01:41:07.835
our two great societies
have always lived in peace.

01:41:07.937 --> 01:41:09.837
- Ah.
- The Trade Federation...

01:41:09.939 --> 01:41:12.135
has destroyed all that we
have worked so hard to build.

01:41:12.242 --> 01:41:15.541
If we do not act quickly,
all will be lost forever.

01:41:15.646 --> 01:41:17.876
I ask you to help us.

01:41:17.981 --> 01:41:20.712
No, I beg you to help us.

01:41:20.819 --> 01:41:23.185
We are
your humble servants.

01:41:25.657 --> 01:41:29.185
Our fate
is in your hands.

01:41:29.295 --> 01:41:31.786
Mmm.

01:41:34.134 --> 01:41:35.761
[Whimpers]

01:41:38.572 --> 01:41:40.096
[Boss Nass Sighs]

01:41:40.240 --> 01:41:43.142
Ha!
[Laughing]

01:41:46.447 --> 01:41:50.714
Yousa no tinken yousa
greater den da Gungans?

01:41:50.819 --> 01:41:53.083
[Chuckling]

01:41:53.188 --> 01:41:57.090
Me-e-esa lika dis!

01:41:57.192 --> 01:41:59.024
Maybe...

01:41:59.129 --> 01:42:01.654
wesa...

01:42:01.765 --> 01:42:03.665
bein friends.

01:42:03.767 --> 01:42:05.998
[Blubbering]

01:42:06.137 --> 01:42:08.731
[All Cheering, Shouting]

01:42:08.873 --> 01:42:11.774
Yippee!
Ya-hoo!

01:42:11.876 --> 01:42:14.209
We've sent
our patrols.

01:42:14.312 --> 01:42:17.804
We already located
their starship in the swamp.

01:42:17.916 --> 01:42:20.077
It won't be long,
my lord.

01:42:20.185 --> 01:42:23.349
This is an unexpected move
for her.

01:42:23.456 --> 01:42:25.481
It's too aggressive.

01:42:25.591 --> 01:42:28.025
Lord Maul, be mindful.

01:42:28.127 --> 01:42:30.688
Let them
make the first move.

01:42:30.798 --> 01:42:32.698
Yes, my master.

01:42:36.170 --> 01:42:37.866
Deysa comin!

01:42:37.972 --> 01:42:40.338
All right!

01:42:42.243 --> 01:42:44.144
They're here!

01:42:44.246 --> 01:42:46.146
Good.
They made it.

01:42:50.719 --> 01:42:52.620
Yousa doen grand.

01:42:52.722 --> 01:42:56.624
- [Chuckles]
- JarJar bring uss-en
and da Naboo together.

01:42:56.726 --> 01:42:58.626
Ah, no, no, no.

01:42:58.728 --> 01:43:01.721
So, wesa make you...

01:43:01.833 --> 01:43:03.858
bombad general.

01:43:03.968 --> 01:43:06.334
General?

01:43:06.437 --> 01:43:08.338
[Moaning]

01:43:08.440 --> 01:43:10.408
- [Qui-Gon] Captain.
- [Laughing]

01:43:10.509 --> 01:43:13.137
- Your Highness.
- What is the situation?

01:43:13.278 --> 01:43:15.179
Almost everyone's
in camps.

01:43:15.281 --> 01:43:18.512
A few hundred police and guards
have formed an underground
resistance movement.

01:43:18.618 --> 01:43:21.178
I brought back as many
of the leaders as I could.

01:43:21.287 --> 01:43:25.952
The Federation army's also much larger
than we thought, and much stronger.

01:43:26.060 --> 01:43:30.360
Your Highness, this is a battle
I do not think that we can win.

01:43:30.464 --> 01:43:32.365
The battle
is a diversion.

01:43:32.467 --> 01:43:35.664
The Gungans must draw the droid army
away from the cities.

01:43:35.770 --> 01:43:38.330
- R2.
- [Beeps]

01:43:38.440 --> 01:43:42.036
We can enter the city using the secret
passages on the waterfall side.

01:43:42.144 --> 01:43:44.044
Once we get to
the main entrance,

01:43:44.146 --> 01:43:46.945
Captain Panaka
will create a diversion.

01:43:47.084 --> 01:43:50.019
Then we can enter the palace
and capture the viceroy.

01:43:50.120 --> 01:43:53.385
Without the viceroy,
they will be lost and confused.

01:43:53.490 --> 01:43:55.391
What do you think,
MasterJedi?

01:43:55.493 --> 01:43:57.654
The viceroy will be
well-guarded.

01:43:57.762 --> 01:44:00.162
The difficulty is getting
into the throne room.

01:44:00.265 --> 01:44:02.700
Once we're inside,
we shouldn't have a problem.

01:44:02.801 --> 01:44:07.534
There is a possibility, with this
diversion, many Gungans will be killed.

01:44:07.640 --> 01:44:10.974
Wesa ready to do
our-san part.

01:44:11.077 --> 01:44:14.205
[Amidala] We have a plan which
should immobilize the droid army.

01:44:14.314 --> 01:44:16.214
We will send
what pilots we have...

01:44:16.316 --> 01:44:19.343
to knock out the droid control ship
orbiting the planet.

01:44:19.487 --> 01:44:22.547
A well-conceived plan.
However, there's great risk.

01:44:22.690 --> 01:44:25.592
The weapons on your fighters
may not penetrate the shields.

01:44:25.694 --> 01:44:27.594
[Obi-Wan]
There's an even bigger danger.

01:44:27.696 --> 01:44:29.596
If the viceroy escapes,
Your Highness,

01:44:29.698 --> 01:44:31.928
he will return
with another droid army.

01:44:32.034 --> 01:44:35.266
Well, that is why we must not
fail to get the viceroy.

01:44:35.371 --> 01:44:37.498
Everything depends on it.

01:44:38.575 --> 01:44:41.170
[Beeps, Whistles]

01:44:42.613 --> 01:44:45.207
She is more foolish
than I thought.

01:44:45.316 --> 01:44:50.254
We are sending all troops to meet
this army assembling near the swamp.

01:44:50.355 --> 01:44:53.017
It appears to be made up
of primitives.

01:44:53.158 --> 01:44:55.683
This will work
to our advantage.

01:44:55.827 --> 01:44:58.626
I have your approval
to proceed, then, my lord?

01:44:58.731 --> 01:45:01.131
Wipe them out.

01:45:02.835 --> 01:45:04.736
All of them.

01:45:18.853 --> 01:45:21.721
[Bellowing]

01:45:35.606 --> 01:45:37.506
Halt!

01:45:40.444 --> 01:45:42.708
Starting up the shield.

01:45:55.862 --> 01:45:58.764
[Rumbling]

01:46:03.037 --> 01:46:05.972
[Loud Whirring]

01:46:11.880 --> 01:46:13.438
Open fire.

01:46:28.865 --> 01:46:32.768
Once we get inside, you find
a safe place to hide and stay there.

01:46:32.904 --> 01:46:34.804
- Sure.
- Stay there.

01:46:39.445 --> 01:46:41.106
[Droids Squawking]

01:46:50.790 --> 01:46:52.849
Roger. Roger.

01:47:00.868 --> 01:47:03.963
I thought the battle was going
to take place far from here.

01:47:04.072 --> 01:47:06.563
This is too close.

01:47:11.748 --> 01:47:13.215
Ani, find cover.

01:47:15.084 --> 01:47:17.349
- Quick!
- Get to your ships!

01:47:29.634 --> 01:47:31.465
Aah!

01:47:37.109 --> 01:47:41.137
[Whistling, Beeping]

01:47:43.750 --> 01:47:45.684
Aah!

01:47:47.020 --> 01:47:49.216
[Continues Beeping]

01:48:02.938 --> 01:48:04.429
[Beeps]

01:48:16.120 --> 01:48:18.520
- Fighters straight ahead.
- Roger, Bravo Leader.

01:48:18.622 --> 01:48:19.851
Roger, Bravo Leader.

01:48:27.700 --> 01:48:29.600
Cease fire.

01:48:34.006 --> 01:48:37.067
[Murmuring]

01:48:37.177 --> 01:48:39.543
Steady. Steady.

01:49:12.717 --> 01:49:15.881
- Activate the droids.
- Yes, sir.

01:49:32.439 --> 01:49:34.339
Ouch time.

01:49:48.424 --> 01:49:50.790
Fire!

01:49:50.893 --> 01:49:53.021
Whoa-ohh!

01:50:03.474 --> 01:50:05.738
Aah! Whoa!

01:50:11.150 --> 01:50:13.675
My guess is the viceroy's
in the throne room.

01:50:13.786 --> 01:50:17.188
Red group! Blue group!
Everybody, this way!

01:50:17.290 --> 01:50:19.281
Hey, wait for me!

01:50:19.392 --> 01:50:21.792
Stay where you are.
You'll be safe there.

01:50:21.895 --> 01:50:24.296
- But l...
- Stay in that cockpit.

01:50:36.111 --> 01:50:39.343
- We'll handle this.
- We'll take the long way.

01:50:46.890 --> 01:50:48.858
[Beeps]

01:50:59.537 --> 01:51:01.471
We gotta do something, R2.

01:51:21.863 --> 01:51:24.161
[Continues Beeping]

01:51:24.265 --> 01:51:27.235
I'm trying to!
I don't know where the trigger is!

01:51:30.539 --> 01:51:33.737
Oops, wrong one.
Maybe it's this one.

01:51:33.877 --> 01:51:35.111
Nope. Wait.
Here it is.

01:51:35.111 --> 01:51:37.204
Nope. Wait.
Here it is.

01:51:38.448 --> 01:51:40.916
Yeah!

01:51:45.790 --> 01:51:48.281
Let's go!

01:51:48.392 --> 01:51:50.623
It's on automatic pilot.

01:51:59.672 --> 01:52:03.005
- Try to override it.
-[R2-D 2 Beeping]

01:53:01.108 --> 01:53:03.576
We don't have time
for this, Captain.

01:53:07.516 --> 01:53:09.575
[Beeping]

01:53:09.684 --> 01:53:11.549
Look! There they are.

01:53:11.653 --> 01:53:14.019
That's where
the autopilot's taking us.

01:53:24.701 --> 01:53:27.761
Huh? Waaah!
Aah! Aah!

01:53:27.871 --> 01:53:29.771
Aah!

01:53:29.873 --> 01:53:33.708
Aaah! Hmm!
Dumb droid. Take that!

01:53:33.811 --> 01:53:37.042
Get off! Get off!
Get off! Get off!

01:53:37.148 --> 01:53:39.083
Ooh! Ooh! Mooie!

01:53:39.185 --> 01:53:41.483
Whoo-hoo! Aah!

01:53:47.093 --> 01:53:49.459
The deflector shield
is too strong.

01:53:57.838 --> 01:54:00.102
- [Whistles]
- This is tense!

01:54:01.543 --> 01:54:04.444
Whoa! R2, get us
off this autopilot.

01:54:04.546 --> 01:54:06.741
It's gonna
get us both killed.

01:54:06.848 --> 01:54:10.842
- [Continues Beeping]
- You did it, R2!

01:54:10.954 --> 01:54:12.615
Okay, let's go left.

01:54:15.725 --> 01:54:18.490
- [Continues Beeping]
- Go back?

01:54:18.596 --> 01:54:22.896
Qui-Gon told me to stay in this cockpit,
so that's what I'm gonna do.

01:54:29.808 --> 01:54:32.276
I'll try spinning.
That's a good trick.

01:54:32.377 --> 01:54:34.346
Whoa!

01:54:36.315 --> 01:54:40.480
- [Whistles]
- I know we're in trouble. J ust hang on.

01:54:47.294 --> 01:54:49.320
Go!

01:54:53.167 --> 01:54:54.862
Ascension guns!

01:56:26.506 --> 01:56:30.341
[Force Field
Humming, Buzzing]

01:56:52.068 --> 01:56:53.593
[Whistles]

01:57:01.012 --> 01:57:02.639
Retreat! Retreat!

01:57:04.416 --> 01:57:06.316
Dis is nutsen.

01:57:06.451 --> 01:57:08.386
Hyah!

01:57:09.655 --> 01:57:11.520
O-O-Ohh!

01:57:16.229 --> 01:57:18.197
Uh-oh.
Big boomers.

01:57:18.298 --> 01:57:20.960
Ohh! Ohh!

01:57:22.202 --> 01:57:23.669
[Gasps]

01:57:25.573 --> 01:57:27.734
Uh-oh! Aaah!

01:57:27.842 --> 01:57:29.901
[Whimpering]

01:57:36.418 --> 01:57:38.818
Hey! Hey!

01:57:38.921 --> 01:57:42.517
Give me a lift!
Aaah! Oh!

01:57:43.660 --> 01:57:45.685
Aaah!

01:57:46.830 --> 01:57:48.492
Ohh!

01:57:48.599 --> 01:57:50.226
JarJar, usen da booma!

01:57:50.334 --> 01:57:52.268
What?
Mesa no have a booma!

01:57:52.369 --> 01:57:54.337
Here. Taken dis one.

01:57:54.438 --> 01:57:57.499
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!
Whoa! Whoa! Aah!

01:57:58.710 --> 01:58:00.337
Aah! Aah! Aah!

01:58:00.445 --> 01:58:03.438
Whoa-ohh!

01:58:03.549 --> 01:58:05.449
Oh! Oh! Oh!

01:58:05.551 --> 01:58:07.041
Aaah!

01:58:07.153 --> 01:58:09.383
Help me!

01:58:10.490 --> 01:58:13.949
JarJar!
J ump, JarJar, jump!

01:58:16.463 --> 01:58:18.591
[Blubbering]

01:58:23.638 --> 01:58:26.904
Put down your weapons.
They win this round.

01:58:37.821 --> 01:58:39.686
[Shrieks]

01:58:39.789 --> 01:58:41.951
We're hit, R2!
Aah!

01:58:43.728 --> 01:58:45.218
[Whistling]

01:58:46.998 --> 01:58:49.262
Aaah!

01:58:53.372 --> 01:58:55.067
[Beeping]

01:58:55.173 --> 01:58:58.166
I'm trying to stop!
I'm trying to stop!

01:59:03.349 --> 01:59:05.284
[Beeps]

01:59:05.386 --> 01:59:06.910
Everything's overheated.

01:59:07.021 --> 01:59:10.354
-[R2-D 2 Beeps]
- Oops. This is not good.

01:59:55.942 --> 01:59:59.811
No!

02:00:22.438 --> 02:00:24.964
No giben up,
General JarJar.

02:00:25.075 --> 02:00:26.975
Mesa tink
of something.

02:00:27.111 --> 02:00:29.545
- Hands up.
- My give up.

02:00:29.647 --> 02:00:31.548
- My give up.
- [Groans]

02:00:40.226 --> 02:00:43.354
Your little insurrection
is at an end, Your Highness.

02:00:43.462 --> 02:00:47.365
Time for you to sign the treaty and end
this pointless debate in the senate.

02:00:47.467 --> 02:00:49.264
Viceroy!

02:00:49.369 --> 02:00:51.303
Your occupation here
has ended.

02:00:52.839 --> 02:00:56.207
After her.
This one's a decoy.

02:01:02.818 --> 02:01:05.378
Captain!

02:01:12.996 --> 02:01:15.590
Jam the doors.

02:01:18.402 --> 02:01:21.963
Now, Viceroy,
we will discuss a new treaty.

02:02:10.761 --> 02:02:13.162
[Groans]

02:02:24.209 --> 02:02:26.507
-[R2-D 2 Beeps]
- Yes! We have power.

02:02:26.612 --> 02:02:29.081
Shields up.

02:02:30.917 --> 02:02:32.578
Take this!

02:02:33.953 --> 02:02:36.388
And this!

02:02:36.490 --> 02:02:38.390
Whoa!

02:02:42.963 --> 02:02:44.864
- Oops.
- We're losing power.

02:02:44.966 --> 02:02:48.163
- There seems to be a problem
with the main reactor.
- Impossible!

02:02:48.270 --> 02:02:50.170
Nothing can get
through our shield.

02:02:51.440 --> 02:02:54.170
- Let's get outta here.
- [Beeping]

02:03:01.318 --> 02:03:03.946
What's that?
It's blowing up from the inside!

02:03:06.958 --> 02:03:08.516
We didn't hit it.

02:03:11.629 --> 02:03:15.157
- Now, this is Podracing.
- [Whistles]

02:03:15.301 --> 02:03:19.032
- Look, one of ours,
out of the main hold!
- Whoo!

02:03:23.476 --> 02:03:26.445
- Whoo!
- Yeah!
- Hee-hee!

02:03:36.724 --> 02:03:39.853
- [Motors Winding Down]
- What the...

02:03:39.962 --> 02:03:42.226
Was'n they doing?

02:03:42.331 --> 02:03:45.893
The control ship has
been destroyed. Look!

02:03:47.637 --> 02:03:50.003
They all broke-ed.

02:03:50.106 --> 02:03:53.007
[All Hooting, Cheering]

02:04:15.101 --> 02:04:16.933
[Grunts]

02:04:19.106 --> 02:04:22.337
[Groans]

02:04:38.394 --> 02:04:41.796
[Muttering]
No, it... it's too late.

02:04:41.898 --> 02:04:44.230
- No.
- Obi-Wan.

02:04:45.502 --> 02:04:47.367
Promise...

02:04:47.470 --> 02:04:49.701
Promise me
you will train the boy.

02:04:49.807 --> 02:04:51.707
Yes, Master.

02:04:55.379 --> 02:04:58.372
He is the chosen one.

02:04:58.517 --> 02:05:01.748
He... will bring balance.

02:05:02.955 --> 02:05:04.856
Train him.

02:05:31.887 --> 02:05:33.718
Now, Viceroy,

02:05:33.823 --> 02:05:37.225
you're going to have to go back
to the senate and explain all this.

02:05:38.962 --> 02:05:42.262
I think you can kiss your
trade franchise good-bye.

02:05:55.981 --> 02:05:59.509
We are indebted to you for
your bravery, Obi-Wan Kenobi.

02:05:59.652 --> 02:06:01.552
And you,
young Skywalker.

02:06:01.654 --> 02:06:05.614
We will watch your career
with great interest.

02:06:12.166 --> 02:06:14.761
Congratulations on your election,
Chancellor.

02:06:14.870 --> 02:06:18.306
Your boldness has saved
our people, Your Majesty.

02:06:18.407 --> 02:06:20.807
It's you who should be
congratulated.

02:06:20.909 --> 02:06:24.812
Together we shall bring peace
and prosperity to the Republic.

02:06:29.219 --> 02:06:34.282
Confer on you the level of
Jedi knight the council does.

02:06:34.425 --> 02:06:39.159
But agree with your taking this boy
as your Padawan learner...

02:06:39.264 --> 02:06:41.164
I do not.

02:06:41.266 --> 02:06:43.325
Qui-Gon believed in him.

02:06:43.435 --> 02:06:45.700
[Sighs]

02:06:45.805 --> 02:06:48.706
The chosen one
the boy may be.

02:06:48.808 --> 02:06:50.708
Nevertheless,

02:06:50.810 --> 02:06:53.712
grave danger I fear
in his training.

02:06:53.814 --> 02:06:57.341
Master Yoda,
I gave Qui-Gon my word.

02:06:57.451 --> 02:06:59.351
I will train Anakin.

02:06:59.419 --> 02:07:01.820
Ohh!
[Grunting]

02:07:01.923 --> 02:07:04.824
Without the approval of the council,
if I must.

02:07:04.926 --> 02:07:07.326
Qui-Gon's defiance
I sense in you.

02:07:07.462 --> 02:07:09.363
Need that you do not.

02:07:11.467 --> 02:07:14.732
Agree with you
the council does.

02:07:15.839 --> 02:07:19.138
Your apprentice
Skywalker will be.

02:07:21.177 --> 02:07:23.077
[Sighs]

02:07:40.166 --> 02:07:42.566
[Whimpers, Beeps]

02:07:46.272 --> 02:07:48.741
What will happen to me now?

02:07:48.842 --> 02:07:51.902
The council have granted me
permission to train you.

02:07:52.012 --> 02:07:55.414
You will be a Jedi,
I promise.

02:08:04.226 --> 02:08:07.252
There's no doubt
the mysterious warrior was a Sith.

02:08:07.363 --> 02:08:10.800
Mmm.
Always two there are.

02:08:10.901 --> 02:08:13.995
No more, no less.

02:08:14.137 --> 02:08:16.867
A master
and an apprentice.

02:08:17.007 --> 02:08:18.908
But which
was destroyed?

02:08:19.010 --> 02:08:21.945
The master
or the apprentice?

02:08:29.888 --> 02:08:33.119
[Crowd Cheering]

02:08:46.574 --> 02:08:48.633
Hello, everybody!

02:08:48.776 --> 02:08:51.371
[Chuckling]

02:09:01.791 --> 02:09:04.693
[Continues]

02:09:07.965 --> 02:09:11.423
- [Growls]
-[Children Laughing]

02:09:35.295 --> 02:09:37.230
Peace!

02:09:37.331 --> 02:09:40.164
- Ya-hoo!
- [Cheering Continues]

02:09:47.442 --> 02:09:48.932
[Beeping]
9:07,965 --> 02:09:11,423
- [Growls]
-[Children Laughing]

02:09:47.442 --> 02:09:48.932
[Beeping]
